/* English translations of archive descriptions, records 1–160. Original records remain unchanged. */
Object.assign(window.NUO_EN = window.NUO_EN || {}, {
  "清傩戏“招魂使者面具，傩戏《章文显》剧中武将面具。呈长方形，头戴红色官帽，额部刻竖式椭圆形，黑面，火焰眉，撇嘴，面部两侧大垂耳。通体刷漆，面貌狰狞，形象似乎是人与鬼的结合，暴凸的眼球大而圆，虎视眈眈，给人以威慑感。": "A Qing-dynasty ‘Soul-Summoning Envoy’ Nuo mask, used for a military character in the Nuo play Zhang Wenxian. Rectangular in shape, it has a red official’s hat, a vertical oval carved on the forehead, a black face, flame-shaped eyebrows, a downturned mouth and large drooping ears. Painted throughout, its fierce face seems to combine human and ghostly traits. Large, round, bulging eyes stare threateningly, creating an intimidating presence.",
  "该面具为安徽傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Anhui Nuo theater or ritual, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "木雕《寿翁》 祁门傩舞面具 谢润华作品。寿翁词语读音:寿(shòu)翁(wēng)词典解释:1.对被祝寿者的尊称。2.高寿的男子。": "Wood carving, Elder of Longevity, a Qimen Nuo dance mask by Xie Runhua. Shouweng (shòu wēng) means: 1. a respectful term for someone receiving birthday wishes; 2. a man of advanced age.",
  "木雕《财神》 祁门傩舞面具 谢润华作品。财神在中国民俗中是主管世间财源的神明。迎财神接财神是中国民间古老的传统节日习俗,供奉财神希望得到财神的眷顾护佑。": "Wood carving, God of Wealth, a Qimen Nuo dance mask by Xie Runhua. In Chinese folk belief, the God of Wealth governs worldly prosperity. Welcoming the deity is an ancient festive custom; worshippers make offerings in the hope of receiving favor and protection.",
  "木雕《魁星》 祁门傩舞面具 谢润华作品。魁星是中国古代星宿名称，是中国古代神话中所说的主宰文章兴衰的神，在儒士学子心目中，魁星具有至高无上的地位。": "Wood carving, Kui Xing, a Qimen Nuo dance mask by Xie Runhua. Kui Xing is the name of an ancient Chinese asterism and, in mythology, a deity governing literary achievement. He holds a supremely important place in the minds of Confucian scholars and students.",
  "木雕《关公品茗》 祁门傩舞面具 谢润华作品。关公，也就是关羽，是东汉末年的名将，被后世尊称为“武圣”。他忠诚勇猛，与刘备、张飞结为兄弟，共同征战天下。在民间，关公被视为忠义、勇武的象征，深受人们敬仰。": "Wood carving, Lord Guan Tasting Tea, a Qimen Nuo dance mask by Xie Runhua. Lord Guan, or Guan Yu, was a celebrated general of the late Eastern Han, honored by later generations as the Martial Sage. Loyal and brave, he became sworn brothers with Liu Bei and Zhang Fei and fought alongside them. In folk tradition, he is widely revered as a symbol of loyalty, righteousness and martial courage.",
  "东方持国尊天王，梵名“提多罗吒”，中国大乘佛教僧众所云护世四大尊天王之一，主据东方。据中国大乘佛教僧众云东尊王护持三千大千世界国土，是故尊名称作东方持国尊天王。东尊天王据须弥山天东方。法器：持国天王手持一杵（Vajra），也被称为金刚杵。这是一种象征力量和无敌的金属法器，用于驱散邪恶和护持正法。": "Dhritarashtra, the Heavenly King of the East, is one of the Four Heavenly Kings who protect the world in Chinese Mahayana Buddhism. He presides over the east and is said to safeguard the lands of the vast cosmos, hence his title, ‘Heavenly King Who Upholds the Realm.’ He resides on the eastern side of Mount Sumeru. Ritual implement: this record describes him holding a vajra, a metal implement symbolizing strength and invincibility, used to dispel evil and protect the true Dharma.",
  "增长天王，佛教护法四大尊天王之一。“增长中国佛教徒认为能令众生增长善根，护持佛法，故名增长天王。南方增长天王，谓能令众生善根增长，居须弥山南天，普天身像常见为青色，穿甲胄（zhòu），手握慧剑，以保护正法不受侵犯，此尊王护持南瞻部洲。南方增长天王，单单把我们职责之内的事情做得很好还不够，还要天天求进步。不进则退啊！时代永远在进步，所以增长天王告诉我们：我们的道行要增长，品德要增长，乃至学问、智慧、才艺、能力都要增长，包括我们的生活水准也要天天提升。": "Virudhaka, the Heavenly King of the South, is one of Buddhism’s Four Heavenly Kings and guardians of the Dharma. Chinese Buddhists interpret his name, ‘Increase,’ as helping beings grow in goodness and protecting Buddhist teachings. He resides on the southern side of Mount Sumeru, is commonly depicted with a blue-green body and armor, and holds a sword of wisdom to prevent harm to the true Dharma. He protects the southern continent of Jambudvipa. The source draws this lesson from him: doing our assigned duties well is not enough; we should seek improvement every day. To stop advancing is to fall behind. As the times progress, we should develop our spiritual practice, virtue, learning, wisdom, artistic skills and abilities, as well as improve our standard of living.",
  "太阳神，民间信仰中的神灵，中国的传统神话、原始信仰、民间信仰和宗教中的太阳神共有数位，他们分别是：羲和、日主、东君、太阳星君、金乌等。太阳星君 太阳星君又称太阳公、太阳神、日神；汉族民间信仰和道教尊奉的太阳神，主掌太阳；道教尊称“日宫炎光太阳星君”，又称“大明之神”，俗称“太阳帝君”、“太阳公”；人们把每年农历三月十九日定为太阳星君的生日。太阳为众阳之宗、纪岁时之准，昔有朱明、大明、阳乌（亦作暘乌）、金乌、金轮等别称；由於其为恒星之，世人敬称星球为星君，太阳亦被尊称为太阳星君。": "The Sun God is a deity in folk belief. Chinese mythology, early beliefs, folk religion and organized religions include several solar figures, such as Xihe, Rizhu, Dongjun, Taiyang Xingjun and the Golden Crow. Taiyang Xingjun, also called the Sun Lord, Sun God or God of the Day, is venerated in Han Chinese folk belief and Daoism as the ruler of the sun. Daoist titles include ‘Solar Star Lord of the Radiant Sun Palace’ and ‘Deity of Great Brightness’; common names include ‘Solar Emperor’ and ‘Sun Lord.’ His birthday is celebrated on the nineteenth day of the third lunar month. The sun is regarded as the source of yang and a standard for marking seasons and years. Older names include Zhuming, Daming, Yangwu, Jinwu and Jinlun. As a star, it is honored with the title Xingjun, ‘Star Lord.’",
  "中国神话中的风伯，其实就是风神，也称作风师、飞廉、箕伯等等，掌八风消息，通五运之气候。风伯的搭档雨师就是雨神，亦称萍翳、玄冥等。中国古代的风神和雨神起源比较早。《周礼》的《大宗伯》篇称：“以燎祀司中、司命、风师、雨师”。道教认为风伯是一个白发老人，左手持轮，右手执扇，作扇轮子状，称风伯方天君。雨师是个老头，名叫陈天君。风神庙 康熙皇帝的儿子雍正，信奉佛教，由于思想局限的关系，他并不知道风是一种自然现象， 而是觉得风灾是因神灵作祟。雍正六年，皇帝颁旨，命钦天监大臣勘测吉地，在皇宫的东侧建设一座风神庙，正名叫宣仁庙，供奉风神，祈求神灵保佑，使国家和皇宫免遭风灾。": "Fengbo, the Wind Earl of Chinese mythology, is also called Fengshi, Feilian or Jibo. He governs the eight winds and the climatic forces of the five cycles. His companion Yushi, the Rain Master, is also called Pingyi or Xuanming. Wind and rain deities have early origins: the ‘Grand Master of Ceremonies’ chapter of the Rites of Zhou describes burnt offerings to Sizhong, Siming, the Wind Master and the Rain Master. In Daoist accounts, Fengbo is a white-haired elder holding a wheel in his left hand and a fan in his right, as if fanning the wheel, and is called Heavenly Lord Fang. The Rain Master is an elder called Heavenly Lord Chen. The source’s account of the Wind God Temple states that the Yongzheng Emperor, son of Kangxi, was a Buddhist who attributed wind disasters to divine action rather than natural causes. In the sixth year of Yongzheng’s reign, he ordered officials of the Imperial Astronomical Bureau to find an auspicious site east of the palace and build the Xuanren Temple, dedicated to the Wind God, to seek protection for the country and palace from wind disasters.",
  "佛教菩萨名，梵文Maitreya的音译，意译慈氏。在佛教传说中，弥勒菩萨是从佛受记（预言），将来为继承释迦牟尼佛位置成为未来佛的菩萨。民间信仰：中国一些寺庙中供奉的笑口常开弥勒像，依据的是五代时的契此和尚。因传说其人是弥勒的化身，所以后人广塑造像供奉。弥勒信仰在古代中国民间有广泛的影响，分为上生信仰和下生信仰两支，宣扬弥勒菩萨以“与乐和学识广博著称。": "Maitreya is the Sanskrit name of a Buddhist bodhisattva, translated into Chinese as Cishi, ‘the Benevolent One.’ In Buddhist tradition, he has received a prophecy that he will succeed Shakyamuni as the future Buddha. In Chinese folk devotion, the smiling Maitreya images found in some temples are based on the monk Qici of the Five Dynasties period. Because he was believed to be an incarnation of Maitreya, later generations widely made and worshipped images of him. Maitreya devotion had a broad influence in premodern China, with traditions focused on ascending to his heaven and on his future descent. The source describes Maitreya as renowned for bringing joy and for extensive learning.",
  "金童，汉语词语，读音是jīn tóng，意思是仙人的侍童。指天真活泼的男儿童。民间多称呼金童玉女。": "Jintong (jīn tóng), literally ‘golden boy,’ means an immortal’s child attendant and can also refer to an innocent, lively young boy. In folk usage it commonly appears in the pair ‘Golden Boy and Jade Maiden.’",
  "三娘即谭三娘，是毛南族民间信仰的神灵。相传她原来是毛南山乡仪风村龙口屯人，少年丧父，与母亲相依为命，与隔壁村壮族青年韦土地相爱，在中秋节对歌定情。一天傍晚三娘到河边洗菜，被当地土司蒙官看中欲纳为妾，三娘不从。蒙官杀死三娘母亲与韦土地，三娘悲愤至极，将蒙官灌醉，杀之报仇。三娘披麻戴孝来到母亲与韦土地墓前痛哭，突然落入墓中，与土地化成两只美丽的蝴蝶。在还愿法事中有“三娘与土地的双人舞，三娘手拿代表小孩灵魂的红蛋，与土地对唱对舞相亲相爱，小土地穿插其中调笑逗乐，寓意为主家带来吉利，子孙昌盛。三娘傩面具为年轻女神形象，脸部饱满，漆黄色，红唇小口，丹凤细眼，用毛笔绘出细眉毛，大耳垂，戴绘红边帽，帽正前方挂阳刻牌饰。": "Sanniang, or Tan Sanniang, is a deity in Maonan folk belief. Legend places her in Longkou Hamlet, Yifeng Village, in the Maonan hills. After losing her father in childhood, she lived with her mother and fell in love with Wei Tudi, a Zhuang youth from a neighboring village, pledging their love through songs at the Mid-Autumn Festival. One evening, the local chieftain Meng Guan saw her washing vegetables by the river and wanted her as a concubine. She refused. After Meng Guan killed her mother and Wei Tudi, Sanniang, overcome with grief and anger, got him drunk and killed him in revenge. Wearing mourning clothes, she wept at her mother’s and Wei Tudi’s graves, suddenly fell into the grave, and transformed with Tudi into two beautiful butterflies. Vow-fulfillment rites include a duet dance by Sanniang and Tudi. Holding a red egg representing a child’s soul, Sanniang exchanges affectionate songs and dances with Tudi, while Little Tudi interjects comic teasing. The performance signifies good fortune and flourishing descendants for the host family. Her mask depicts a young goddess with a full yellow-painted face, small red lips, slender phoenix-shaped eyes, fine painted eyebrows and large earlobes. A red-edged hat bears a raised plaque ornament at the front.",
  "该面具为毛南族傩面具之瑶王，又称花仙公、白裤瑶公，是白裤瑶祖先的代表。瑶王是一位多子多福的好心人，其妻为瑶婆。相传瑶王原与毛南人一起杂居，后因人多地少，瑶王主动带领族人趟过打狗河，到深山老林生活，从此主管森林。在毛南族民间传说中，有一对毛南族老夫妇向万岁娘娘求花（花代表孩童），归家途中不慎将花遗失，被瑶王拾到，瑶王爬山涉水、历经千辛万苦将拾到的花归还给失主。瑶王傩面具为中年男子形象，面漆红褐色，满脸皱纹，眉开眼笑，露有两颗门牙，可爱亲切。其发式为白裤瑶男子的传统发式，用白布把拧成一股的头发旋紧从脑后盘绕至前额，成为顶在头上的发髻。": "This Maonan Nuo mask depicts the Yao King, also called Huaxian Gong or Baiku Yao Gong, a representative ancestor of the Baiku Yao people. A kind man blessed with many children, he is married to Yao Po. According to legend, he originally lived alongside the Maonan, but when the population grew and land became scarce, he voluntarily led his people across the Dagou River into the deep forests, which he thereafter governed. A Maonan tale recounts an elderly couple who asked Wansui Niangniang for flowers, symbols of children, but lost them on the way home. The Yao King found the flowers and crossed mountains and rivers, enduring great hardship, to return them. His mask depicts a middle-aged man with a reddish-brown, deeply wrinkled face, smiling eyes and eyebrows, and two exposed front teeth, giving a friendly, endearing appearance. His hairstyle follows the traditional Baiku Yao male style: hair twisted into a single lock, wrapped tightly with white cloth, and coiled from the back of the head toward the forehead into a topknot.",
  "该面具为毛南族傩面具之土地，即土地神、土地爷。在毛南族民间传说中，土地是一位勤奋的神差，是功曹的助手，通晓各神驻地，和功曹一起负责帮主家通知各位神仙入筵领愿，为各路神仙清扫路面。毛南族的土地非常人情化，在还愿法事中有“三娘与土地的双人舞，土地遇三娘唱情歌求爱，调笑逗乐，寓意主家子孙兴旺发达。土地傩面具为老年男子形象，面漆红褐色，满脸皱纹，眉开眼笑，长黑胡须遮嘴，露整齐上牙，凹眼弯眉，大耳垂，戴上绿下蓝方高帽，帽正前方红笔写“王字，可爱亲切，喜气洋洋。": "This Maonan Nuo mask depicts Tudi, the Earth God. In Maonan folklore, he is a diligent divine messenger and assistant to Gongcao. Knowing where the deities reside, he helps invite them to the host’s ritual feast to receive vows and sweeps their paths clean. The Maonan Earth God is notably human in character. Vow-fulfillment rites include a duet dance by Sanniang and Tudi, in which he sings love songs, courts her and jokes playfully, expressing wishes for the host family’s descendants to flourish. His mask shows an elderly man with a reddish-brown, deeply wrinkled face, smiling brows and eyes, a long black beard partly covering the mouth, a neat row of upper teeth, recessed eyes, curved eyebrows and large earlobes. He wears a tall square hat, green above and blue below, with the character for ‘king’ written in red on the front. His appearance is friendly and joyful.",
  "该面具为毛南族傩面具之灵娘，在毛南族信奉的神仙中，灵娘是万岁娘娘身边的副官，也是主管人生意兴旺的财神。在毛南族民间传说中，灵娘是一位风流女子，但对平民很好。灵娘傩面具为中年妇女形象，头上的花冠饰金币、禽鸟与荷包，面颊圆润，白面红唇，两道弯眉中间有颗红痣，妩媚动人，十分富态。": "This Maonan Nuo mask depicts Lingniang. Among the deities honored by the Maonan, she is an attendant to Wansui Niangniang and a wealth deity responsible for prosperous business. Folk tales describe her as a flirtatious woman who is kind to ordinary people. Her mask depicts a middle-aged woman with a floral crown decorated with gold coins, birds and embroidered pouches. Rounded cheeks, a white face, red lips and a red mole between curved eyebrows create a charming, prosperous appearance.",
  "该面具为毛南族傩面具之花林仙官，又名“小婆王”，为掌管婚姻生育之神万岁娘娘的助手，是在花山种花管花的护花神。在还愿法事中，花林仙官给主家送银花（女孩），还要给主家孩子的祖母送长生鸡，还愿法事请她入筵，除了请她送花、护花、守花之外，也表示主家对她的 花林仙官傩面具为美丽的年轻女子形象，弯眉秀目，眉心点朱砂，红唇垂耳，皮肤白皙，面颊绯红，头戴的花冠上有笑脸娃娃、花朵和树叶图案。": "This Maonan Nuo mask depicts Hualin Xianguan, also called ‘Little Powang.’ She assists Wansui Niangniang, the deity of marriage and fertility, and tends and protects the flowers on Flower Mountain. In vow-fulfillment rites, she brings silver flowers, representing girls, to the host family and a longevity chicken to the child’s grandmother. She is invited to the ritual feast to deliver, protect and guard flowers. The original account leaves its next statement about the host’s regard for her incomplete. Her mask depicts a beautiful young woman with curved eyebrows, elegant eyes, a cinnabar mark between the brows, red lips, long earlobes, fair skin and rosy cheeks. Her floral crown bears motifs of smiling children, flowers and leaves.",
  "该面具为毛南族傩面具之万岁娘娘，又称花王圣母、圣母娘娘、三尊圣母、婆王、花婆等。在毛南人的心中，万岁娘娘处在最高女神的位置，为掌管婚姻生育之神。毛南族认为万岁娘娘住在花山，管护花山。在毛南族山乡，花是孩童的象征，万岁娘娘送花是赐子于家庭，送红花或金花为赐男孩，送蓝花或银（白）花为赐女孩。人间男女结成姻缘，是万岁娘娘把红花和白花移栽到了一起。旧时毛南人新婚时便在神灵牌位面前许愿，在新房门上挂红布条，插上花枝，算是搭座红桥，表达向神灵寻花求子的心愿。假如婚后多年未育，则举行架桥求花再次向万岁娘娘许愿。待得花有子之后，要择吉日请师公来进行还愿法事。要是小孩体弱多病，则是他在花山上的命花出现了问题，可能是缺水、生虫或缺肥，这时要祭拜万岁娘娘，祈求她好好照顾孩子的命花。人死之后，灵魂会变为花回到万岁娘娘的花山上，待万岁娘娘再次赐花，则投胎转世。万岁娘娘傩面具为红脸老妇形象，面带笑容，皱纹满布，束发戴帽，帽子饰一圈花朵图案和一圈笑脸娃娃图案，红唇垂耳。": "This Maonan Nuo mask depicts Wansui Niangniang, also called Huawang Shengmu, Shengmu Niangniang, Sanzun Shengmu, Powang or Huapo. In Maonan belief she is the highest goddess and governs marriage and childbirth. She lives on and tends Flower Mountain. Flowers symbolize children: a red or golden flower grants a boy, while a blue or silver-white flower grants a girl. Marriage occurs when she transplants a red and a white flower together. Traditionally, newlyweds made vows before divine tablets, hung a red cloth strip above the bridal-room door and inserted flowering branches to form a symbolic red bridge, expressing a wish for children. If a couple remained childless for years, they performed a bridge-building rite to seek flowers and renewed their vows. After a child was born, they chose an auspicious date and invited a ritual master to conduct a vow-fulfillment ceremony. A sickly child was believed to have a life-flower on Flower Mountain suffering from insufficient water, pests or poor nourishment; the family prayed to the goddess to tend it. After death, the soul returned to her mountain as a flower, to be reborn when she bestowed it again. The mask depicts a smiling, red-faced elderly woman with many wrinkles, tied-up hair and a hat decorated with rings of flowers and smiling children, along with red lips and long earlobes.",
  "该面具为毛南族傩面具之“三界公”，又称“三界公爷”，是毛南地区管辖范围最宽、法力最大的一位神灵，也是毛南族最信仰最崇敬的一位善神。过去在毛南山乡村村都有三界庙，每年庙节（即分龙节）要请师公在三界庙前跳木面舞、椎牛献祭给三界公爷。三界傩面具为英俊男子形象，头戴黑色冠帽，帽子中部绘有火焰纹，帽檐绘缠枝花纹，帽子上戴红黄色相间条纹头巾。剑眉细眼，鼻梁笔直坚挺，白面红唇垂耳，蓄有胡须，面容清秀，文质彬彬，有“青龙将军的风范。": "This Maonan Nuo mask depicts Sanjie Gong, also called Sanjie Gongye. He is described as the deity with the widest jurisdiction and greatest powers in Maonan areas, and a benevolent god especially revered by the Maonan. Formerly, every village in the Maonan hills had a Sanjie temple. At the annual temple festival, also called the Fenlong Festival, ritual masters were invited to perform wooden-mask dances and sacrifice cattle before the temple. The mask depicts a handsome man wearing a black headdress with a flame motif at its center, scrolling floral decoration around the brim and a red-and-yellow striped headcloth. Sword-shaped brows, slender eyes, a straight prominent nose, a white face, red lips, long earlobes and a beard create a refined, scholarly appearance reminiscent of the ‘Azure Dragon General.’",
  "瑶王是毛南族跳神中独有的人物，出现在《瑶王捡花踏桥》及《仙官架桥》等剧目中，均为主要角色。": "The Yao King is a figure distinctive to Maonan ritual performances. He is a principal character in plays including The Yao King Finds Flowers and Crosses the Bridge and The Immortal Official Builds a Bridge.",
  "瑶婆也称“瑶王妻”，与瑶王该面具为一对，相传瑶王瑶婆能给愿主带来子嗣与吉祥。此面具敷黑、褐两色，头部雕刻圆髻，比较典型特征是眉毛眼睛下垂，眼珠小而微凸，鼻梁挺直，面部光滑，嘴唇丰润，下巴圆厚，双耳较大，下垂，面具整体呈现慈眉善目中老年妇女形象，采用雕刻手法为浮雕，局部眼珠为透雕。": "Yao Po, also called ‘the Yao King’s Wife,’ forms a pair with the Yao King. Tradition holds that the couple can bring children and good fortune to those fulfilling vows. This mask is painted black and brown, with a round topknot. Its characteristic features are drooping eyebrows and eyes, small slightly protruding pupils, a straight nose, smooth cheeks, full lips, a rounded substantial chin and large drooping ears. The whole presents a kindly middle-aged or elderly woman. The mask is carved in relief, with openwork at the eyes.",
  "莫一大王，相传为广西河池人，因有功于国、有德于民，而被后人尊为神。": "King Moyi is said to have come from Hechi, Guangxi. Later generations revered him as a deity for his service to the country and kindness to its people.",
  "雷公，祈雨以及秋收还大愿用。物极必反，盛极而衰，这是事物的发展规律。我们已经不能亲眼目睹宋代的桂林面具是如何的精美生动，只能凭借文字记载去充分地想象。": "Thunder God, used in rain-seeking rites and major vow-fulfillment ceremonies after the autumn harvest. The source reflects that things turn toward their opposites at their extremes and decline after reaching their height. The exquisite, vivid masks of Song-dynasty Guilin can no longer be seen firsthand; their appearance must be imagined from written accounts.",
  "猪头，舞狮领路用。该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "Pig Head, used to lead the way in a lion dance. This mask carries animal, exorcistic or early ritual associations. Exaggerated mouths, noses, eyes and outlines often convey an intimidating presence.",
  "猴子，舞狮领路用。该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "Monkey, used to lead the way in a lion dance. This mask carries animal, exorcistic or early ritual associations. Exaggerated mouths, noses, eyes and outlines often convey an intimidating presence.",
  "先锋小姐，用于秋收时还大愿活动。该面具表现傩仪中的女性神灵、祖先或家族护佑角色，常与求子、婚育、还愿和祈福主题相关。": "Vanguard Lady, used in major vow-fulfillment ceremonies after the autumn harvest. This mask portrays a female deity, ancestor or family-protecting figure in Nuo ritual, often associated with wishes for children, marriage, childbirth, vow fulfillment and blessings.",
  "艮殿，用于还大愿活动。该面具为广西傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Gendian, used in major vow-fulfillment activities. A character mask from Guangxi Nuo theater or ritual, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "天皇，用于还大愿活动。该面具为广西傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Tianhuang, used in major vow-fulfillment activities. A character mask from Guangxi Nuo theater or ritual, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "仙公，主管五谷、雨水，驱野兽，保佑年丰岁足之神。": "Xiangong, a deity who governs grain and rainfall, drives away wild animals and blesses the year with abundance.",
  "赵元帅，道教护法，师公舞驱瘟仪式时出现。": "Marshal Zhao, a Daoist guardian who appears in epidemic-expelling rituals of Shigong dance.",
  "茶酒，师公舞面具，用于秋收时还大愿活动。": "Tea and Wine, a Shigong dance mask used in major vow-fulfillment activities after the autumn harvest.",
  "足高，用于还大愿活动。该面具为广西傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Zugao, used in major vow-fulfillment activities. A character mask from Guangxi Nuo theater or ritual, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "三界公爷，左边是最下面一层，右边是戴上了夹层。": "Sanjie Gongye. The left image shows the innermost layer; the right shows the mask with an intermediate layer fitted.",
  "该面具为令公李靖，唐初大将。据记载，面具的最外面一层是本相，为红色，代表令公的威武庄严；中间是善相，为白色，代表着令公的仁慈和蔼；最里层是凶相，为金色，代表着令公的威慑力量。": "This mask depicts Lord Li Jing, an early Tang general. According to the record, the outermost layer is his true aspect, colored red to express martial dignity; the middle layer is his benevolent aspect, colored white to express kindness; and the innermost is his fierce aspect, colored gold to express intimidating power.",
  "该面具为广西傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Guangxi Nuo theater or ritual, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "苗族，清代，长25厘米，宽7.5厘米，厚10厘米，木质，20世纪50年代征集于广西南丹。敷红、黑、黄三彩上漆。和尚面具宽脸长耳，细眉细目，似笑非笑，额头雕刻有红色福包，为傩戏角色之一，雕刻工艺为浮雕和透雕。": "Miao, Qing dynasty. Wood, 25 cm long, 7.5 cm wide and 10 cm thick; collected in Nandan, Guangxi, in the 1950s. Painted and lacquered in red, black and yellow. This monk mask has a broad face, long ears, fine eyebrows and narrow eyes, with an ambiguous smile. A red auspicious bulge is carved on the forehead. It is a Nuo theater character, carved using relief and openwork techniques.",
  "苗族清代土地神傩戏面具。该面具对应民间信仰中的神祇角色，多与护佑地方、祈福禳灾、风雨收成或仪式迎神有关。": "A Qing-dynasty Miao Earth God mask for Nuo theater. The mask corresponds to a deity in folk belief, often associated with local protection, blessings and the averting of disaster, weather and harvests, or ritual welcomes for deities.",
  "清代苗族土川官傩戏面具。该面具为广西傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A Qing-dynasty Miao Tuchuan Guan mask for Nuo theater. A character mask from Guangxi Nuo theater or ritual, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "壮族龙牙歪面具是中国广西壮族自治区壮族文化中的一种独特的民族工艺品，它以其独特的造型和深厚的文化内涵而闻名。": "The Zhuang Longyawai mask is a distinctive craft object in the culture of the Zhuang people of Guangxi, China, known for its unusual form and rich cultural associations.",
  "陈咬金地戏面具 ” 地戏由于剧目丰富、人物众多，面具的造型也更为丰富，大体可分为五类，包括主将、道人、丑角、动物和世俗人物。其中主将在地戏中占有极其重要的地位，不但有正派、反派之分，还有文将、武将、老将、少将和女将之别。程咬金，字义贞，原名咬金，后更名知节。在地戏唱本《薛仁贵征东》和《薛丁山征西》中，均有程咬金的出场。程咬金被认为是福将，所以在地戏面具的刻画上，在嘴角两侧雕刻上一堆蝙蝠，以取“福的谐音。又因为程咬金在唐代算是长寿之人，故尔额头上刻一寿星，带给人福寿双全的吉祥含义。": "A Cheng Yaojin Dixi mask. Dixi’s extensive repertoire and many characters give rise to varied mask forms, broadly grouped as leading generals, Daoists, comic characters, animals and secular figures. Leading generals hold a particularly important place and include heroes and villains, civil and martial commanders, old and young generals, and female generals. Cheng Yaojin, courtesy name Yizhen, later changed his personal name to Zhijie. He appears in Dixi scripts including Xue Rengui Campaigns East and Xue Dingshan Campaigns West. Regarded as a fortunate general, he is depicted with bats carved beside his mouth, punning on fu, ‘good fortune.’ Because he was long-lived by Tang-dynasty standards, a Longevity Star figure is carved on his forehead, conveying the auspicious wish for both good fortune and long life.",
  "刘备（161年-223年6月10日），字玄德，东汉末年幽州涿郡涿县（今河北省涿州市）人，西汉中山靖王刘胜之后，三国时期蜀汉开国皇帝，年号章武。": "Liu Bei (161–10 June 223), courtesy name Xuande, came from Zhuo County, Zhuo Commandery, You Province, in the late Eastern Han, now Zhuozhou, Hebei. A descendant of Liu Sheng, Prince Jing of Zhongshan in the Western Han, he founded the Shu Han state during the Three Kingdoms period and ruled under the era name Zhangwu.",
  "张飞（?-221年），字益德（《三国演义》中字翼德），东汉末年幽州涿郡（今河北省保定市涿州市）人氏，三国时期蜀汉名将。": "Zhang Fei (died 221), courtesy name Yide, written with a different first character in Romance of the Three Kingdoms, came from Zhuo Commandery, You Province, in the late Eastern Han, now Zhuozhou, Baoding, Hebei. He was a celebrated Shu Han general during the Three Kingdoms period.",
  "岳飞，宋代爱国名将，传说他是天上大鹏星转世投胎，所以，其头盔刻画有大鹏展翅的造型。藏品。": "Yue Fei, the celebrated patriotic Song-dynasty general, was said to be a reincarnation of the celestial Great Peng Star. His helmet therefore bears the form of a great peng bird with outspread wings. A collection object.",
  "周武王” 周武王姬发（？―约公元前1043年），姬姓，名发。周文王姬昌与太姒的嫡次子，岐周（今陕西岐山）人，西周王朝的开国君主。周文王姬昌时期，国力逐渐强大，“天下三分，其二归周”，为灭商奠定了基础。姬昌崩逝后，其子姬发继位，史称周武王。姬发对内重用贤良，继续以姜太公（即姜尚）为军师，并用弟弟周公旦为太宰，召公、毕公、康叔、丹季等良臣均各当其位，人才荟萃，政治蒸蒸日上。对外争取联合更多诸侯国，壮大力量。武王审时度势，积极为灭商准备条件，等待时机。为便于进攻商都朝歌，周武王在沣水东岸建立新都镐京（今陕西省西安市）。": "King Wu of Zhou, personal name Ji Fa (died around 1043 BCE), was the second legitimate son of King Wen, Ji Chang, and Tai Si. From Qizhou, now Qishan, Shaanxi, he founded the Western Zhou dynasty. Under King Wen, Zhou grew so powerful that ‘of the world’s three portions, two belonged to Zhou,’ laying the groundwork for overthrowing Shang. Ji Fa succeeded his father as King Wu, retaining Jiang Taigong, or Jiang Shang, as military adviser and appointing his younger brother the Duke of Zhou, Dan, as chief minister. The Duke of Shao, Duke of Bi, Kang Shu, Dan Ji and other capable officials served in suitable posts, strengthening governance. He also sought alliances with more regional states. Assessing the situation, he prepared for Shang’s overthrow and awaited the right moment. To facilitate an attack on the Shang capital Chaoge, he established Haojing, now in Xi’an, Shaanxi, as a new capital on the east bank of the Feng River.",
  "费仲，费氏，名中（亦作仲），祖先嬴姓，商朝末期人物，帝辛的姑舅亲表弟。牧野之战当天他和商朝兵将与姬周拼个鱼死网破，被周兵偷袭战死沙场。费仲是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，与尤浑并为纣王身边的佞臣。": "Fei Zhong, whose name is written with either of two characters pronounced Zhong, belonged to the Fei lineage with ancestral surname Ying. A late Shang figure, he was a maternal cousin of King Di Xin. The account states that on the day of the Battle of Muye he fought alongside Shang troops against Zhou and was killed in a surprise attack. In the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods, he and You Hun are corrupt advisers serving King Zhou of Shang.",
  "武吉是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，为姜子牙的四个弟子之一，同门一师的师弟为龙须虎、五路神、魏贲。乃一介凡人，本是樵夫出身，后为西周做出了一定贡献。之后周文王碰见武吉，武吉引文王见姜太公，其受封为“武德将军一职，成为周军四大先锋之一的右哨，师徒二人后为周文王效力，讨伐商纣王。": "Wu Ji is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods and one of Jiang Ziya’s four disciples, alongside Longxuhu, Wulushen and Wei Ben. A mortal originally employed as a woodcutter, he later contributed to the Western Zhou cause. After encountering King Wen, he introduced him to Jiang Taigong. Appointed ‘General of Martial Virtue,’ he became the right-flank member of Zhou’s four vanguard commanders. Master and disciple served King Wen in the campaign against King Zhou of Shang.",
  "该面具为贵州安顺傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Nuo theater or ritual in Anshun, Guizhou, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "黄天爵(觉)，男，中国明代神仙小说《封神演义》之中的虚拟人物，武成王黄飞虎与贾氏夫人的第三子，祖父为黄滚，长兄为黄天化、次兄为黄天禄，弟弟为黄天祥。姑母为黄娘娘(纣王之妃)，叔父为黄飞彪、黄飞豹。黄天爵是黄飞虎第三子，与十二岁随武成王反商投奔西岐。后来伐纣时因父亲丧子，回西岐服侍祖父黄滚。": "Huang Tianjue is a male fictional character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. He is the third son of Huang Feihu, King Wucheng, and Lady Jia; his grandfather is Huang Gun. His elder brothers are Huang Tianhua and Huang Tianlu, and his younger brother is Huang Tianxiang. His aunt is Lady Huang, a consort of King Zhou of Shang, and his uncles are Huang Feibiao and Huang Feibao. At twelve, he followed his father in rebelling against Shang and joining Xiqi. Later, during the campaign against King Zhou, after his father lost a son, Tianjue returned to Xiqi to care for his grandfather Huang Gun.",
  "白礼是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的虚拟人物。所属截教门人，为金鳌岛十天君之一。闻仲讨伐西岐，到金鳌岛请来十天君，摆下了“十绝阵”。白礼布下“烈焰阵”，乃“十绝阵的第七阵。此阵被陆压道人所破，白礼死于阵中。死后封神榜上封雷部二十四位天君之一。": "Bai Li is a fictional character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. A member of the Jie sect, he is one of Golden Turtle Island’s Ten Heavenly Lords. When campaigning against Xiqi, Wen Zhong invited the ten lords to establish the Ten Deadly Formations. Bai Li set up the seventh, the Fierce Flame Formation. The Daoist Lu Ya broke it, and Bai Li died inside. After death, he was invested as one of the Thunder Department’s Twenty-Four Heavenly Lords.",
  "张绍是明代神妖小说《封神演义》中的虚拟人物之一，截教门人，金鳌岛十天君之一。是十绝阵之一\"红沙阵\"的阵主。": "Zhang Shao is a fictional character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. A Jie sect disciple and one of Golden Turtle Island’s Ten Heavenly Lords, he commands the Red Sand Formation, one of the Ten Deadly Formations.",
  "该面具表现历史、小说或民间戏曲中的武将人物，通常用于突出忠勇、威严或护卫性的角色身份。": "This mask portrays a military figure from history, fiction or folk theater, usually emphasizing loyalty, courage, authority or a protective role.",
  "明代小说《封神演义》人物，姚宾是截教门人，金鳌岛十天君之一。闻仲讨伐西岐，到金鳌岛请来十天君，摆下了\"十绝阵\"。姚宾布下\"落魂阵\"，乃\"十绝阵\"的第八阵。刚到西岐时，姚宾用拜草人之法术头顶催魂灯，脚下促魂灯拜走姜尚二魂六魄，姜尚魂游昆仑山被赤精子借来太极图抢走草人抢回魂魄救活姜尚。刚刚投奔西周的方相死于阵中，后来被赤精子所破，并用阴阳镜杀死姚宾。死后封神榜上封雷部二十四位天君之一。": "Yao Bin is a character in the Ming-dynasty novel Investiture of the Gods, a Jie sect disciple and one of Golden Turtle Island’s Ten Heavenly Lords. When Wen Zhong campaigned against Xiqi, he invited the ten lords to establish the Ten Deadly Formations. Yao Bin set up the eighth, the Soul-Felling Formation. On arriving at Xiqi, he used a straw effigy and soul-compelling lamps above and below it to draw away two of Jiang Shang’s hun souls and six po souls. As Jiang’s soul wandered on Mount Kunlun, Chi Jingzi borrowed the Taiji Diagram, seized the effigy and recovered the souls, restoring him to life. Fang Xiang, who had just joined Western Zhou, died in the formation. Chi Jingzi later broke it and killed Yao Bin with the Yin-Yang Mirror. After death, Yao Bin was invested as one of the Thunder Department’s Twenty-Four Heavenly Lords.",
  "董全，是明代神怪小说《封神演义》中的虚拟人物，是截教门人，金鳌岛十天君之一。闻仲讨伐西岐，到金鳌岛请来十天君，他摆下了\"十绝阵\"之一的\"风吼阵\"。死后封神榜上封雷部二十四位天君之一。": "Dong Quan is a fictional character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods, a Jie sect disciple and one of Golden Turtle Island’s Ten Heavenly Lords. Wen Zhong invited the ten lords to aid his campaign against Xiqi, and Dong Quan established the Howling Wind Formation, one of the Ten Deadly Formations. After death, he was invested as one of the Thunder Department’s Twenty-Four Heavenly Lords.",
  "当代安顺地戏面具《封神榜》高青青是一件由贵州省民族博物馆通过征集而来的民族历史和文化藏品。": "The contemporary Anshun Dixi mask Gao Qingqing, from Investiture of the Gods, is an object of ethnic history and culture acquired for the collection of the Guizhou Provincial Museum of Ethnology.",
  "当代安顺地戏面具《封神榜》杨禁是一件由贵州省民族博物馆通过征集而来的民族历史和文化藏品。": "The contemporary Anshun Dixi mask Yang Jin, from Investiture of the Gods, is an object of ethnic history and culture acquired for the collection of the Guizhou Provincial Museum of Ethnology.",
  "伯安，是1990版《封神榜》里的原创人物，为西伯侯姬昌第三子，原著并无此人，由刘昌伟饰演。当代安顺地戏面具《封神榜》勃安是一件由贵州省民族博物馆通过征集而来的民族历史和文化藏品。伯安，90版《封神榜》原创角色，西伯侯姬昌第三子，心术不正，偏又爱出风头，且为人轻佻，先后受叔父姬遂和申公豹的蛊惑，合谋刺杀姬发，阴谋败露，被姬昌贬为庶民，但伯安仍不知悔改，主动投靠商军，表示愿意与商军里应外合，自己继承西伯侯。带刺客意图行刺，未成功，抓走了王后商青君，用以要挟西岐军。哪吒请缨潜入商军营寨救援，见商青君被绑在帐中的柱子上，伯安出言调戏遭呵斥后欲行非礼，哪吒救了商青君，在打斗中杀死伯安。": "Bo An is an original character in the 1990 television adaptation of Investiture of the Gods, played by Liu Changwei. He is Ji Chang’s third son and does not appear in the novel. The contemporary Anshun Dixi mask Bo An, from Investiture of the Gods, is an object of ethnic history and culture acquired by the Guizhou Provincial Museum of Ethnology. In the television story, Bo An is frivolous, ambitious and dishonest. Influenced first by his uncle Ji Sui and then by Shen Gongbao, he conspires to assassinate Ji Fa. When the plot is exposed, Ji Chang demotes him to commoner status. Unrepentant, he joins the Shang army and offers to coordinate an attack from within so that he can inherit the title of Western Lord. After an unsuccessful assassination attempt, he abducts Queen Shang Qingjun as a hostage against Xiqi. Nezha volunteers to rescue her from the Shang camp. Finding her tied to a tent post, Nezha intervenes when Bo An, rebuffed after taunting her, attempts to assault her. He rescues Shang Qingjun and kills Bo An in the fight.",
  "魔礼海，长约二丈四尺，武器为一杆长枪。法宝为碧玉琵琶，琵琶有四根弦，分别为地、 水、火、风四弦，也可召唤黑风、火蛇，风助火势，席卷战场。魔礼海地戏面具是一件由贵州省民族博物馆通过征集。魔礼海是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，魔家四将之一，用一根长枪，背上一把碧玉琵琶，上有四条弦，按“地火水风排布，拨动琴弦，风火齐至，与青云剑有异曲同工之妙，后也被黄天化用攒心钉穿心而亡。死后封为四大天王之北方多文天王，职雨。": "Mo Lihai is described as about two zhang and four chi tall and carries a long spear. His magical jade pipa has four strings representing earth, water, fire and wind; it can summon black winds and fiery snakes that sweep the battlefield, with wind intensifying the flames. This Dixi mask of Mo Lihai was acquired by the Guizhou Provincial Museum of Ethnology. Mo Lihai is one of the four Mo-family generals in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. He bears a spear and a jade pipa whose strings are arranged as earth, fire, water and wind. Plucking them summons wind and fire, like the powers of the Qingyun Sword. Huang Tianhua later kills him with the Heart-Piercing Nail. After death, he is invested as the Northern Heavenly King of Extensive Learning, one of the Four Heavenly Kings, responsible for rain.",
  "石天君是封神榜中的角色。他是截教门人，本名石矶，与太乙真人是师兄弟。他住在骷髅山白骨洞，曾收服了三名弟子，分别是碧云童子、彩云童子和虬首仙。": "Heavenly Lord Shi is presented here as a character in Investiture of the Gods. The record calls him a Jie sect disciple originally named Shi Ji, a fellow disciple of Taiyi Zhenren, living in White Bone Cave on Skull Mountain. It names three disciples: Biyun Tongzi, Caiyun Tongzi and Qiushouxian.",
  "黄飞豹是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，界牌关总兵黄滚之子，殷商武成王黄飞虎的三弟，家传枪法，性急如火。在嫂子和妹妹被纣王杀害后，劝说哥哥黄飞虎反商，反出朝歌，闯出五关，投奔西岐，后来每次作战都跟随黄飞虎。武王伐纣过黄河逢梅山七怪，邬文化夜袭周营，黄飞豹死于乱军之中（也可能死于纣王之手）。姜子牙岐山封神，封其为天嗣星。": "Huang Feibao is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. He is the son of Huang Gun, commander of Jiepai Pass, and the younger brother of Shang’s King Wucheng, Huang Feihu. Skilled in his family’s spear techniques and fiery in temper, he urges Huang Feihu to rebel after King Zhou kills their sister and Huang Feihu’s wife. They flee Chaoge, break through five passes and join Xiqi; thereafter Feibao accompanies his brother in battle. During King Wu’s campaign against Shang, after crossing the Yellow River and encountering the Seven Monsters of Mount Mei, Wu Wenhua attacks the Zhou camp at night. Huang Feibao dies in the confusion; the record also gives King Zhou as a possible cause of death. At the investiture on Mount Qi, Jiang Ziya appoints him the Tiansi Star.",
  "羽翼仙是《封神演义》中的人物，原形是一只大鹏金翅雕，从蓬莱岛而来。后成为阐教仙人燃灯道人的二弟子，是李靖同门一师的师弟。羽翼仙具有扇干四海之水的强大法力，试图想以北海之水淹没西岐，后被元始天尊以三光神水阻止，燃灯道人追踪到羽翼仙的踪迹，便诱使饥饿的羽翼仙连吃自己一百零八个念珠后，将其收服，后为了保命便拜燃灯道人为师。成为燃灯道人的门人兼坐骑，后来还曾协助燃灯道人大战商朝大将孔宣，结果被打败而归，后文再无出现。": "Yuyi Xian, the Winged Immortal in Investiture of the Gods, is originally a golden-winged great peng bird from Penglai Island. He later becomes the second disciple of the Chan sect immortal Randeng Daoren, a fellow disciple junior to Li Jing. With the power to fan the four seas dry, he attempts to flood Xiqi with water from the northern sea, but Yuanshi Tianzun stops him using Three Lights Divine Water. Randeng tracks him down and induces the hungry bird to swallow his 108 prayer beads, thereby subduing him. To save his life, Yuyi Xian accepts Randeng as his master and becomes both disciple and mount. He later helps Randeng fight the Shang general Kong Xuan but is defeated, and does not appear again in the narrative.",
  "陶荣是神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物。本是黄花山占山为王的土匪野将之一。因为商朝太师闻仲讨伐西岐路过黄花山，将其与结义兄弟邓忠、辛环、张节四将一并收服，跟随闻仲一同出征。陶荣本是黄花山占山为王的土匪。陶荣擅使双锏，有法宝聚风幡，一旦摇动霎时间飞砂走石，播土扬尘，天昏地暗。他是一位法力拥有法宝又武艺超群的将军。后来“十绝阵被破，赵公明和三宵娘娘、十天君先后阵亡。姜子牙率军半夜劫营，陶荣把守左营，被黄飞虎之子黄天祥所杀，死后封神榜上封雷部二十四位天君之一。因是凌霄宝殿玉皇大帝镇殿大将。掌管风雷水火之职。（。": "Tao Rong is a character in Investiture of the Gods, originally a bandit commander on Huanghua Mountain. When Shang’s Grand Preceptor Wen Zhong passes through on his campaign against Xiqi, he subdues Tao Rong and his sworn brothers Deng Zhong, Xin Huan and Zhang Jie, who join his army. Tao Rong uses a pair of metal truncheons and a magical Wind-Gathering Banner; shaking it sends sand, stones and dust flying and darkens the sky. He combines martial skill with magical powers. After the Ten Deadly Formations are broken and Zhao Gongming, the Three Xiao Goddesses and the Ten Heavenly Lords have fallen, Jiang Ziya launches a night attack. Guarding the left camp, Tao Rong is killed by Huang Tianxiang, son of Huang Feihu. After death, he becomes one of the Thunder Department’s Twenty-Four Heavenly Lords, a guardian general of the Jade Emperor’s Lingxiao Palace with duties over wind, thunder, water and fire.",
  "辛环是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，是闻仲太师在黄花岭所收的邓、辛、张、陶四天君之一。兵器为一对雷公凿的锤钻，本事与雷震子无二，都生有一双翅膀，可以飞天作战。最终死于雷震子的棍下， 姜子牙归国封神，封辛环为雷部二十四位天君正神，属于雷公一职。辛环，原本与邓忠、张节、陶荣占据黄花山，书中按表此四人武艺高强，身怀绝技与法宝，尤其是辛环，生得非凡人。他背生一对双翅，面如红枣色，嘴生獠牙，一手持锤，一手持钻，飞行若鸾鸟。在《封神演义》中但凡长得似人非人的，一般都有点身份背景，但这辛环却没交代，仿佛就是天生地养的，属于野生。他实力比殷商、西岐众多人类将领肯定要高，不然闻仲不会收在自己麾下。": "Xin Huan is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods, one of the four commanders Deng, Xin, Zhang and Tao recruited by Wen Zhong at Huanghua Ridge. He uses a thunder-god hammer and chisel and, like Lei Zhenzi, has wings for aerial combat. Lei Zhenzi eventually kills him with a staff. Jiang Ziya later invests him as one of the Thunder Department’s Twenty-Four Heavenly Lords, serving as a thunder deity. Originally occupying Huanghua Mountain with Deng Zhong, Zhang Jie and Tao Rong, Xin Huan is described as especially extraordinary among these skilled warriors with special abilities and magical treasures. With wings on his back, a red-jujube-colored face and fangs, he flies like a luan bird while carrying hammer and chisel. The source comments that, unlike many part-human figures in the novel, he has no explained supernatural lineage and seems to have arisen naturally. It considers him stronger than many human generals of Shang and Xiqi, which would account for Wen Zhong recruiting him.",
  "马善是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，原本是阐教仙人燃灯道人琉璃灯里的灯芯之火，生有三眼，私逃下凡做强盗，和温良结义，占山为王，被商太子殷郊所收服，并随殷郊一起攻打西岐，在追赶姜子牙时，最终被燃灯道人亲自收回。马善本为燃灯道人的琉璃灯之火，私逃下凡后，和强盗温良结义，占山为王。其戴扇云盔，身披淡黄袍，手持点铁枪，骑着白龙马；长得面如傅粉，三绺长髯，有三只眼，住在白龙山。与温良一起跟随商太子殷郊讨伐西岐，被周将邓九公活擒，姜子牙下令斩首，依仗法力，即砍即生，又遭众玉虚弟子以三昧真火焚烧，不但毫发无伤，而且借火遁而去。杨戬用照妖镜照出马善的原形，查清根源，燃灯道人亲自下凡，用琉璃灯收走了灯芯马善。": "Ma Shan is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. Originally the flame of the wick in Randeng Daoren’s glass lamp, he has three eyes and escapes to the mortal world, where he becomes a bandit and sworn brother of Wen Liang. Shang’s prince Yin Jiao recruits them to attack Xiqi; while pursuing Jiang Ziya, Ma Shan is finally reclaimed by Randeng. The account describes him wearing a Fanyun helmet and pale yellow robe, carrying a metal spear and riding a white dragon horse. He has a powdered-looking face, three long locks of beard and three eyes, and lives on White Dragon Mountain. Fighting alongside Wen Liang under Yin Jiao, he is captured by Zhou general Deng Jiugong. Jiang Ziya orders his execution, but each time his head is cut off it grows back. The Jade Void disciples burn him with Samadhi True Fire, yet he is unharmed and escapes through the flames. Yang Jian reveals his original form with a demon-revealing mirror; Randeng descends in person and draws the lamp-wick spirit back into his glass lamp.",
  "邓忠是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，殷商闻仲太师西征姜子牙时，于黄花山收得的邓辛张陶四将之首，其生的面如蓝靛，发似朱砂，巨口獠牙，声如霹雳，使一柄开山斧，勇猛异常。邓忠，又称邓元帅，是九天应元雷声普化天尊部下的天神，常以邓元帅为首。《夷坚志补》卷二三：“宗室赵善蹈，少时遇九华周先生传灵宝大法，行持多显效。筑坛行法，见神人火焰绕身，曰：“吾天元考召邓将军也。”宋代称之为“天元邓将军”。明姚宗仪《常熟志》记载，致道观有雷神殿。前以“律令大神邓元帅为首。另外，《封神演义》中称为邓忠，《西游记》中称为邓化，都是指邓元帅。": "Deng Zhong is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods and leader of the four generals Deng, Xin, Zhang and Tao recruited by Wen Zhong on Huanghua Mountain during his western campaign against Jiang Ziya. With an indigo face, cinnabar-red hair, a huge fanged mouth and a thunderous voice, he wields a mountain-splitting axe with exceptional courage. Also called Marshal Deng, he is a heavenly general under the Nine Heavens’ Universal Transformer of Thunder, often leading that deity’s generals. Volume 23 of the Supplement to Yijian Zhi relates that Zhao Shandao learned Lingbao rites from Master Zhou of Jiuhua in his youth and saw many effective results. During a ritual, a divine figure surrounded by flames appeared and declared, ‘I am General Deng of Tianyuan, who examines and summons.’ In the Song he was called General Deng of Tianyuan. Yao Zongyi’s Ming-dynasty Changshu Gazetteer records a Thunder God Hall at Zhidao Temple, led by ‘Marshal Deng, Great Deity of Commands.’ The source identifies Deng Zhong in Investiture of the Gods and Deng Hua in Journey to the West as the same Marshal Deng.",
  "赵江是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，截教门人，为金鳌岛十天君之一。赵江布下“地烈阵”，乃“十绝阵的第二阵。赵江被武吉杀死后，在封神榜上被封雷部二十四位天君之一。": "Zhao Jiang is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods, a Jie sect disciple and one of Golden Turtle Island’s Ten Heavenly Lords. He establishes the Earth-Blazing Formation, the second of the Ten Deadly Formations. After Wu Ji kills him, he is invested as one of the Thunder Department’s Twenty-Four Heavenly Lords.",
  "陈奇是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，哼哈二将中的“哈将”。为商纣王的部将之一，青龙关总兵丘引的督粮官，手使一根荡魔杵。为助纣为虐的武将，座下有三千飞虎兵，坐骑也是火眼金睛兽，其外形与拿人手段也似郑伦一般，武艺也如郑伦相当。陈奇曾受异人秘传，养成腹中一道黄气，张口一哈，黄气喷出，见之者魂魄自散。曾喷出黄气生擒邓九公、太鸾、黄天禄、土行孙。败给莲花化身的哪吒；与郑伦是敌对关系，初次和郑伦交战时，两者各使摄魂异术，二人同时攻击，结果两方互相中招落马，被各自的下属抢救而回，以此逗乐了观战的群众，这是封神演义中比较搞笑的一段情节。": "Chen Qi is the ‘Ha General’ of the Heng-Ha pair in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. A subordinate of King Zhou of Shang, he supervises provisions for Qiu Yin, commander of Qinglong Pass, and wields a demon-subduing pestle. Supporting the tyrant, he commands 3,000 Flying Tiger soldiers and rides a beast with fiery eyes and golden pupils. His appearance, fighting ability and means of capturing opponents resemble Zheng Lun’s. A mysterious teacher secretly taught him to cultivate a yellow vapor in his abdomen: shouting ‘Ha’ releases it, scattering the souls of those who see it. He captures Deng Jiugong, Tai Luan, Huang Tianlu and Tu Xingsun this way, but loses to Nezha’s lotus-body incarnation. In his first fight with his enemy Zheng Lun, both use soul-capturing powers simultaneously, knock one another from their mounts and are rescued by their own troops. The spectators find this amusing; the source calls it one of the novel’s comic episodes.",
  "秦完是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，截教门人，为金鳌岛十天君之一。闻仲讨伐西岐，到金鳌岛请来十天君，摆下了“十绝阵”。秦完布下“天绝阵”，乃“十绝阵之首。此阵曾演先天之数，得先天清气，内藏混沌之几，中有三首幡，按天、地、人三才，共合为一气。若人入此阵内，有雷鸣之处，化作灰尘；仙道若逢此处，肢体震为粉碎。阐教门人邓华死于阵中，后来被文殊广法天尊所破，并用遁龙桩将秦完杀死。死后封神榜上封雷部二十四位天君之一。": "Qin Wan is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods, a Jie sect disciple and one of Golden Turtle Island’s Ten Heavenly Lords. Wen Zhong invites the ten lords to establish the Ten Deadly Formations against Xiqi. Qin Wan creates the first, the Heaven-Extinguishing Formation. Based on primordial numbers and pure primordial qi, it contains the workings of chaos and three banners corresponding to heaven, earth and humanity, united as one vital force. A mortal entering it turns to dust at the sound of thunder, while an immortal’s limbs are shattered. The Chan sect disciple Deng Hua dies within it. Wenshu Guangfa Tianzun later breaks the formation and kills Qin Wan with the Dragon-Binding Pillar. After death, Qin Wan becomes one of the Thunder Department’s Twenty-Four Heavenly Lords.",
  "黄滚是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，商朝的镇边老帅，界牌关守将。武成王黄飞虎的父亲，次子为黄飞彪，三子为黄飞豹。女儿为黄妃（纣王之妃），儿媳妇为贾氏。孙子为黄天化、黄天禄、黄天爵、黄天祥。": "Huang Gun is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods, a veteran Shang frontier commander guarding Jiepai Pass. He is the father of Huang Feihu, King Wucheng; his other sons are Huang Feibiao and Huang Feibao. His daughter is Consort Huang, wife to King Zhou of Shang, and his daughter-in-law is Lady Jia. His grandsons are Huang Tianhua, Huang Tianlu, Huang Tianjue and Huang Tianxiang.",
  "陈奇是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，哼哈二将中的“哈将”。为商纣王的部将之一，青龙关总兵丘引的督粮官，手使一根荡魔杵。陈奇是哼哈二将中的“哈将”。陈奇曾受异人秘传，养成腹中一道黄气，张口一哈，黄气喷出，见之者魂魄自散。曾喷出黄气生擒邓九公、太鸾、黄天禄、土行孙。败给莲花化身的哪吒；与郑伦是敌对关系，初次和郑伦交战时，两者各使摄魂异术，二人同时攻击，结果两方互相中招落马，被各自的下属抢救而回，以此逗乐了观战的群众，这是封神演义中比较搞笑的一段情节。": "Chen Qi is the ‘Ha General’ of the Heng-Ha pair in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. A subordinate of King Zhou of Shang, he supervises provisions for Qiu Yin, commander of Qinglong Pass, and carries a demon-subduing pestle. A mysterious teacher taught him to cultivate yellow vapor in his abdomen; shouting ‘Ha’ releases it, scattering the souls of those who see it. He captures Deng Jiugong, Tai Luan, Huang Tianlu and Tu Xingsun with this power but loses to Nezha’s lotus-body incarnation. In his first encounter with his enemy Zheng Lun, both use their soul-capturing powers at once, fall from their mounts and are rescued by their own followers. The spectators are amused; the source describes this as one of the novel’s comic episodes.",
  "孙寅是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物。": "Sun Yin is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods.",
  "姬昌，又称周文王，是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，原为商朝西伯侯，是伯邑考、周武王姬发之父。姬昌原为殷商西伯侯，是商纣王东西南北的四大伯侯之一，乃一代文臣明主，居住于西岐国土，其家室庞大妻妾众多，且生有大量子嗣（小说中特别多次强调姬昌的妻儿众多，共有百子），又奇遇逢生，虽有七年之厄，但之后福缘深厚，且有推算预知的道术绝技，西岐家乡有雄兵四十万，战将六十员。": "Ji Chang, also known as King Wen of Zhou, is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. Originally the Western Lord under Shang, he is the father of Bo Yikao and Ji Fa, later King Wu of Zhou. One of Shang’s four great regional lords, he is portrayed as a wise ruler and civil minister living in Xiqi. He has a large household with many wives, concubines and children; the novel repeatedly emphasizes his hundred sons. Despite a seven-year ordeal, he survives extraordinary encounters and later enjoys great good fortune. He possesses Daoist divination skills that allow him to foresee events. His homeland of Xiqi has 400,000 soldiers and sixty generals.",
  "散宜生，古典神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，“文王四友之一。通过权臣费仲、尤浑游说纣王，救出了文王。后来又辅佐武王伐纣。": "San Yisheng is a character in the classical fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods and one of King Wen’s Four Friends. By persuading King Zhou through the powerful advisers Fei Zhong and You Hun, he secures King Wen’s release. He later assists King Wu in the campaign against Shang.",
  "释迦牟尼佛，本是古印度迦毗罗卫国(今尼泊尔境内)的太子，属刹帝利种姓。父为净饭王，母为摩耶夫人，佛为太子时名叫\"乔达摩·悉达多\"，意为\"一切义成就者\"(旧译\"义成\")。历史几百年来，安顺的民间艺人以木为纸，以凿为笔，凭着精湛的雕刻技艺，制作出了一件件雄浑粗犷、神色各异的面具。备注 部分、第三方平台， 秦发忠傩雕面具作品。": "Shakyamuni Buddha was originally a prince of Kapilavastu in ancient India, in present-day Nepal, belonging to the Kshatriya caste. His father was King Shuddhodana and his mother Queen Maya. As a prince he was named Siddhartha Gautama, interpreted as ‘one who accomplishes every aim.’ For centuries, folk artists in Anshun have treated wood as paper and chisels as brushes, using accomplished carving skills to create powerful, rugged masks with varied expressions. Record note: some material comes from third-party platforms; Nuo mask carving by Qin Fazhong.",
  "吞口是云、贵、川、湘等省一些少数民族地区挂在门楣上，用于驱邪的木雕，大多以兽头为主，也有人兽结合的，还有挂葫芦或木瓢的。缘由 将吞口悬挂在大门的门楣上方，避邪镇宅，平日里俯视、监视门前，一旦有妖鬼进门，便一口把它吞下，这也是被人们唤我“吞口的缘故。备注 部分、第三方平台， 秦发忠傩雕面具作品。": "Tunkou are wooden carvings hung above doors to ward off evil in some ethnic communities of Yunnan, Guizhou, Sichuan, Hunan and other provinces. Most depict animal heads; others combine human and animal forms, or use gourds or wooden ladles. Hung over the entrance, a Tunkou protects the home and watches the doorway. If a demon or ghost enters, it is believed to swallow it in one bite, giving the object its name, ‘swallowing mouth.’ Record note: some material comes from third-party platforms; Nuo mask carving by Qin Fazhong.",
  "贵州安顺地戏鱼嘴道人面具。该面具为贵州安顺傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A Fish-Mouthed Daoist mask from Anshun Dixi, Guizhou. A character mask from Nuo theater or ritual in Anshun, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "贵州安顺地戏面具鱼嘴道人， 角色：反派 出处：鱼嘴道人出现在安顺地戏《薛丁山征西》中，由鱼精变化而成，阻碍薛丁山西征。": "Fish-Mouthed Daoist, an Anshun Dixi mask from Guizhou. Role: antagonist. Source: in the Anshun Dixi play Xue Dingshan Campaigns West, he is a transformed fish spirit who obstructs Xue Dingshan’s western campaign.",
  "关羽、张飞、杨继业那细腻的线条、鲜明的色彩，仿佛是岁月精心雕琢的杰作。博览馆面积有180平方米，共分四个展馆。展馆内，面具脸谱共110个、收藏的地戏唱本共23册，馆内还有多个朝代的帅旗、战旗、兵器等。地址：安顺市普定县 定南街道 金马新村 村委会办公室内。": "Guan Yu, Zhang Fei and Yang Jiye: their fine lines and vivid colors evoke works carefully shaped by time. The exhibition hall covers 180 square meters and is divided into four galleries. It contains 110 masks, 23 collected Dixi scripts, and command flags, battle flags and weapons from several dynasties. Address: village committee office, Jinma New Village, Dingnan Subdistrict, Puding County, Anshun.",
  "兰陵王本名高长恭，北齐皇室成员，他爹是文襄帝高澄。公元541年，他生于北齐皇族成员，文襄帝高澄的第四子。兰陵王，形象狰狞，头上一只神鸟，环形豹眼，一个大美傩面。": "The Prince of Lanling, Gao Changgong, was a member of the Northern Qi royal family and the fourth son of Emperor Wenxiang, Gao Cheng, born in 541. This fierce-looking Nuo mask has a sacred bird above the head and round leopard-like eyes, creating an imposing appearance.",
  "兰陵王的长相，“貌柔心壮，音容兼美”，长得跟个漂亮大姑娘似的，外貌娇嫩，内心却很强大。在古代两军对垒，那都是刀光剑影、杀气腾腾，细皮嫩肉、跟姑娘似的将领，往往都会被对方藐视，难以鼓舞士气，为了不让敌人小瞧，兰陵王想出个招儿，弄了个狰狞恐怖的面具。每次上战场，就把这面具一戴，瞬间从美男子变身威严的 形象，非常的狰狞，让人恐惧和后怕。": "The Prince of Lanling was described as ‘gentle in appearance but strong in heart, with a beautiful voice and face.’ His delicate features were compared to those of a beautiful young woman, although he was inwardly strong. On an ancient battlefield filled with flashing blades and hostility, such a youthful-looking commander could be underestimated by enemies and struggle to inspire his troops. To avoid being dismissed, the prince devised a frightening, ferocious mask. Wearing it into battle transformed his handsome appearance into an intimidating figure that inspired fear.",
  "关于兰陵王这个面具，很多人都不了解，又似乎很熟悉他的传说故事。邙山之战战役之后，兰陵王名声大噪，兰陵王从此名留青史。兰陵王本名高长恭，公元541年，他生于北齐皇族成员，文襄帝高澄的第四子。兰陵王傩面，形象狰狞，头上一只神鸟，环形豹眼。": "Many people know little about the Prince of Lanling mask but are familiar with his legend. His fame spread after the Battle of Mangshan, securing his place in history. His personal name was Gao Changgong. Born in 541 into the Northern Qi royal family, he was Emperor Wenxiang Gao Cheng’s fourth son. The Prince of Lanling Nuo mask has a fierce appearance, a sacred bird above the head and round leopard-like eyes.",
  "贵州遵义道真傩戏面具人物“铁匠” ， 铁匠是一门古老的职业，他们以铁为原料，靠一把小小的铁锤打造出各式各样的生产工具和生活用品来养家糊口。面具。": "The Blacksmith, a Nuo theater mask character from Daozhen, Zunyi, Guizhou. Blacksmithing is an ancient trade: working with iron and a small hammer, blacksmiths forge tools and everyday objects to earn a living.",
  "该面具为贵州遵义傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Nuo theater or ritual in Zunyi, Guizhou, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "傩公，红脸男性，傩的主要人物，任何一坛傩戏首先要在傩堂正中供奉，才能保佑这坛傩戏顺利进行，也才能达到主家的目的。傩公傩母，是傩坛上供奉的正神，一般又被认为代表着伏羲与女娲。": "Nuo Gong is a red-faced male and a principal figure in Nuo. Before any Nuo performance cycle, he is enshrined at the center of the ritual hall to protect its smooth progress and help fulfill the host’s purpose. Nuo Gong and Nuo Mu are principal deities honored on the altar and are generally also understood as representing Fuxi and Nüwa.",
  "判官是封建社会时期的官名，始于隋朝。至唐，节度使、观察使、防御使均置判官，为地方长官的僚属，辅理政事。": "Panguan, ‘judge,’ was an official title in imperial China, first used in the Sui dynasty. In the Tang, military governors, surveillance commissioners and defense commissioners appointed panguan as staff officials who assisted with administration.",
  "唐上元 唐、葛、周三元面具均采用正神面相造型，但面具头盔部分造型有文有武，其中唐上元面具采用文官帽饰。": "Tang Shangyuan. The masks of the Three Yuan deities Tang, Ge and Zhou all use the facial form of principal deities, while their headwear varies between civil and military styles. Tang Shangyuan wears a civil official’s hat.",
  "婆王圣母，也称“花婆圣母”“花王圣母”“万岁天尊圣母等等，是“做桥系统中的主要神灵之一。相传远古时，婆王圣母原为高王三公主，为神话人物盘瓠之妻，产下六男六女，共十二姓，分居黔中、湘西一带。其头饰有娃娃纹样，与其司职有一定关系。": "Powang Shengmu, also called Huapo Shengmu, Huawang Shengmu or Wansui Tianzun Shengmu, is a principal deity in the ‘bridge-making’ ritual system. According to legend, she was originally King Gao’s third princess and wife of the mythic Panhu. She bore six sons and six daughters, giving rise to twelve surnames that settled across central Guizhou and western Hunan. The child motifs on her headdress are related to her divine responsibilities.",
  "圆脸秃头，龇牙咧嘴。笑容可鞠，额上长着一个硕大的“祸色包”，形象可爱。傩戏中有笑和尚、老和尚、小和尚，他们身穿和尚衣，手拿小钹，在傩戏中口念阿弥陀佛，专治心术不正之人。": "Round-faced and bald, with exposed teeth and a broad grin, this endearing figure has a large forehead swelling called a ‘huose bao’ in the record. Nuo theater includes a Laughing Monk, Old Monk and Young Monk. Wearing monks’ robes and holding small cymbals, they recite Amitabha’s name and deal specifically with people of dishonest intent.",
  "民国铜仁龙王傩面具是一件由贵州省民族博物馆通过征集而来的民族历史和文化藏品。面具。": "The Republican-period Dragon King Nuo mask from Tongren is an object of ethnic history and culture acquired for the collection of the Guizhou Provincial Museum of Ethnology.",
  "关羽，《三国演义》名将，忠、义、勇为世人所赞美，因此，逐步被神化，沿海一带奉其为财神爷。关羽面具则注重赤面、凤眼、剑眉的刻绘。面具。": "Guan Yu, the celebrated general in Romance of the Three Kingdoms, is admired for loyalty, righteousness and courage. He gradually became deified and is worshipped as a wealth deity in coastal areas. His masks emphasize a red face, phoenix-shaped eyes and sword-shaped brows.",
  "该面具为贵州铜仁傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Nuo theater or ritual in Tongren, Guizhou, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "《梵净山傩神》傩面具（正面） 《梵净山傩神》傩面具（背面） 《梵净山傩神》傩面具， 梵净山武陵山脉主峰，海拔2572米，位于贵州省铜仁市的江口、印江、松桃三县交界处，总面积为775.14平方千米，遗产地面积402.75平方千米，缓冲区面积372.39平方千米。梵净山是中国南方最早从海洋抬升为陆地的地方之一。": "Nuo Deity of Mount Fanjing, shown from the front and back. Mount Fanjing, the main peak of the Wuling Mountains, rises to 2,572 meters at the junction of Jiangkou, Yinjiang and Songtao counties in Tongren, Guizhou. The overall area is 775.14 square kilometers, comprising a 402.75-square-kilometer heritage area and a 372.39-square-kilometer buffer zone. It is among the earliest places in southern China to have risen from the sea into land.",
  "关羽，《三国演义》名将，忠、义、勇为世人所赞美，因此，逐步被神化，沿海一带奉其为财神爷。地戏中关羽面具则注重赤面、凤眼、剑眉的刻绘。": "Guan Yu, the celebrated general in Romance of the Three Kingdoms, is admired for loyalty, righteousness and courage. He gradually became deified and is worshipped as a wealth deity in coastal areas. In Dixi, his masks emphasize a red face, phoenix-shaped eyes and sword-shaped brows.",
  "龙须虎是地戏《封神榜》中周营的战将，最后被封为九丑星。在名著《封神演义》中因为形象特殊、个性讨喜且屡建奇功，深受民间读者的喜爱。龙须虎身世离奇，据说是龙与豹子结合而生，因此在地戏面具龙须虎的额上有一只龙头，口鼻被做成虎豹之型。": "Longxuhu is a Zhou army general in the Dixi play Investiture of the Gods, eventually invested as the Nine-Ugliness Star. In the novel, his unusual appearance, appealing personality and repeated extraordinary achievements made him popular with readers. His origin is said to lie in the union of a dragon and a leopard. Dixi masks therefore place a dragon’s head on his forehead and give his mouth and nose tiger- or leopard-like forms.",
  "贵州狮虎面具均以木材制作而成，比一般直接佩戴的傩神面具要大出许多，所以一般在面具后制作有把手，表演时，舞者手持把手进行表演。贵州狮舞面具额头上会以浮雕工艺雕刻以大大的福包，有的福包上还会刻上象征老虎万兽之王身份的王子纹样，在威风八面的背后还会透出一点虎头虎脑的趣致。舞动时需佩戴下颌，舞者身上还需使用罩布。贵州狮（虎）舞更多的体现了自然淳朴、原始抽象之美。": "Lion and tiger masks from Guizhou are carved from wood and are much larger than Nuo deity masks worn directly on the face. They generally have handles behind them, which dancers hold during performance. Lion dance masks often have a large auspicious swelling carved in relief on the forehead; some also bear the character wang, ‘king,’ signifying the tiger as king of beasts. Beneath their imposing appearance is a playful, endearingly tiger-like quality. Performances require an attached lower jaw and a cloth covering over the dancer’s body. Guizhou lion and tiger dances particularly convey a natural, unadorned and abstract beauty.",
  "杨任在地戏《封神榜》中是周营将领，因苏妲己谗言，纣王昏庸，被迫害失去双眼，冤魂怨气冲天引起一位得道真人注意，被救后眼眶生出双手，手上长眼，获得了上观天庭，下探地穴，中识人间万事的能力，最后得道成仙，助武王伐纣。": "Yang Ren is a Zhou general in the Dixi play Investiture of the Gods. Slandered by Su Daji and persecuted under the foolish King Zhou, he loses both eyes. His spirit’s overwhelming grievance attracts an accomplished Daoist, who rescues him. Hands grow from his eye sockets, with eyes on the palms, allowing him to see heaven above, caverns below and all affairs of the human world. He eventually becomes an immortal and assists King Wu’s campaign against Shang.",
  "钟馗是民间传说中有名的捉鬼、吃鬼、斩鬼大神。传言钟馗的盛行起源于唐明皇梦境，梦中钟馗为唐明皇除去妖孽吃下恶鬼而得到推崇。该面具为清代松桃县面具，刀法圆润，造型独特，表情威严。傩戏剧目之《钟馗斩鬼》。": "Zhong Kui is a famous deity in folk legend who catches, eats and slays ghosts. His popularity is said to originate in Emperor Xuanzong of Tang’s dream, in which Zhong Kui removed evil beings and ate a malicious ghost, earning the emperor’s esteem. This Qing-dynasty mask from Songtao County has rounded carving, a distinctive form and an imposing expression. Associated Nuo play: Zhong Kui Slays the Ghost.",
  "切加法王，藏语读作“荡金曲嘉”，汉语意为法王，是文殊菩萨显化的阎王形象,呈忿怒相。在羌姆表演中，切加法王充当本尊。所谓本 尊就是在同类神祇中以它为首，是级别最高的神明，其它神祇均为臣属。该面具为水牛头造型,三目圆睁,头饰三骷髅冠,二角竖立,张口呲牙卷舌,面目狰狞。白马藏族的切加法王面具以木质雕刻而成，形似牛头，色泽原始古朴，通身暗棕色，头上刻有骷髅冠，牛角直立，透着肃穆与威严。": "Qiejia Fawang, given in Tibetan here as ‘Dangjin Qujia’ and meaning ‘Dharma King,’ is a wrathful form of Yama manifested by Manjushri. In Cham performance he serves as the principal deity, the highest-ranking figure among associated deities, with the others as attendants. The mask takes the form of a water buffalo head, with three wide-open eyes, a three-skull crown, upright horns, exposed teeth and a curled tongue in a fierce open mouth. The Baima Tibetan version is carved from wood. Its buffalo-like head, dark brown coloration, skull crown and erect horns create a solemn, imposing presence.",
  "四川白马藏族的护法神面具造型特征与西藏藏族羌姆面具护法神相似，同样头戴骷髅冠，以五目睥睨世间善恶轮回。面具以木质雕刻而成，线条简约朴素，色彩古朴凝重，与鲜艳的布质或纸质羌姆面具相比，别有一番滋味。": "The guardian-deity masks of the Baima Tibetans in Sichuan resemble those of Tibetan Cham in Tibet: both wear skull crowns and gaze with five eyes upon worldly good, evil and the cycle of rebirth. Carved from wood, with simple lines and restrained, solemn colors, they offer a different aesthetic from brightly colored cloth or paper Cham masks.",
  "“撮泰吉是流行于贵州威宁彝族中的一种原始粗犷的傩戏，其意为“变人戏”，主要反映彝族先民迁徙、农耕和繁衍的历史。该戏一般在每年正月初三至十五的“扫火星民俗活动中演出，旨在驱邪崇，迎吉祥。现为国家级非物质文化遗产代表作。“撮泰吉在整个表演中，只有5具面具，其造型非常原始、简朴，每个面具都有特定的名称。其造型特点为面具呈圆弧形，前额宽阔厚实、眼角上挑、鼻高且直、平板脸；其色彩为黑底，然后再用白色颜料在面具上勾画出线条。": "Cuotaiji is a rugged Nuo theater tradition among the Yi people of Weining, Guizhou. Its name means ‘the drama of becoming human,’ and it primarily recounts ancestral migration, farming and reproduction. It is generally performed during the ‘Sweeping the Fire Stars’ folk activities between the third and fifteenth days of the first lunar month, to expel evil and welcome good fortune. It is now recognized on the national intangible cultural heritage list. Only five masks are used in the full performance, each with a specific name. Their forms are simple and archaic: an arched shape, a broad substantial forehead, upturned eye corners, a high straight nose and a flat face. White lines are painted over a black ground.",
  "莫一大王，本名莫公佞，在莫家六兄弟中排行老大，故而在封神时便被命名为“通天圣帝莫一大王”，此为老年文相造型。": "King Moyi, originally named Mo Gongning, was the eldest of six Mo brothers. On becoming a deity, he was therefore named ‘Heaven-Reaching Sacred Emperor, King Moyi.’ This mask depicts his elderly civil aspect.",
  "张龙是包公身边的带刀护卫，是他的左膀右臂，代表着伸张正义，宣扬公正威严的角色。": "Zhang Long is an armed guard and trusted aide to Judge Bao, representing the defense of justice, impartiality and authority.",
  "麻洪摩 贵州彝族撮泰吉面具 ” 麻洪摩，意为“苗族老人”，已经1200岁。": "Mahongmo, a Cuotaiji mask of the Yi people of Guizhou. The name means ‘Miao Elder,’ said to be 1,200 years old.",
  "阿达姆 贵州彝族撮泰吉面具 ” 阿达姆，意为“老奶奶”，是老爷爷阿布摩的妻子，也是一位长寿的老人，传说已有1500岁。": "Adamu, a Cuotaiji mask of the Yi people of Guizhou. The name means ‘Grandmother.’ She is the wife of Grandfather Abumo, and is also long-lived, said to be 1,500 years old.",
  "招魂使者是贵池傩戏《章文显》的剧中人物，黑面宽口，不怒自威，结合代表着刚烈性格的黑蓝的面色，立刻呈现出一派刚正不阿严肃威猛的神灵官差面相。火红额冠与火焰横眉与面色形成鲜明对比，更是彰显着招魂使者那穿梭于阴阳的刚烈威严的凶神气势。": "The Soul-Summoning Envoy is a character in the Guichi Nuo play Zhang Wenxian. His black face and broad mouth convey authority even without anger. Black and blue-black facial colors, associated here with a forceful temperament, give him the stern, incorruptible appearance of a divine officer. A fiery red forehead crown and horizontal flame-shaped brows contrast sharply with the face, emphasizing the fierce dignity of a powerful being who moves between the worlds of the living and the dead.",
  "贵州狮（虎）舞面具 ” 贵州狮虎面具均以木材制作而成，高宽一般为50公分，比一般直接佩戴的傩神面具要大出许多，所以一般在面具后制作有把手，用在娱乐活动表演中。表演时，舞者手持把手进行操作。": "Guizhou lion and tiger dance masks are made from wood and are generally about 50 cm high and wide, much larger than Nuo deity masks worn directly on the face. They usually have handles behind them and are used in entertainment performances, with dancers manipulating them by hand.",
  "金兀术地戏面具 ” 金兀术，中文名完颜宗弼，金朝名将，能征善战。在地戏唱本《岳飞传》里是重要反派战将之一，与岳飞相互敌对。相传其为赤须龙转世，因此在面具的雕刻上，将龙鼻作为其造型的代表性特征。": "Jin Wuzhu Dixi mask. Jin Wuzhu, whose Chinese name was Wanyan Zongbi, was an accomplished military commander of the Jin dynasty. In the Dixi script The Story of Yue Fei, he is a major antagonist and Yue Fei’s opponent. Said to be the reincarnation of a red-whiskered dragon, he is represented by a distinctive dragon-like nose in the carving.",
  "“撮泰吉为彝语“变人戏的音译，是彝族古老的信仰民俗。阿布摩，意为“老爷爷”，传说他已有1700岁，被视为彝族的祖先，智慧的长者，是撮泰吉中的灵魂人物。在表演中繁衍后代，教会百姓农耕。撮泰吉代表着世代彝族儿女对生命的崇敬、对自然的虔诚的信仰。": "Cuotaiji is a transliteration of a Yi term meaning ‘the drama of becoming human,’ an ancient Yi religious custom. Abumo means ‘Grandfather.’ Said to be 1,700 years old, he is regarded as a Yi ancestor, a wise elder and the central figure in Cuotaiji. In performance he produces descendants and teaches the people to farm. Cuotaiji expresses generations of Yi people’s reverence for life and devotion to nature.",
  "岳飞，宋代爱国名将，传说他是天上大鹏星转世投胎，所以，其头盔刻画有大鹏展翅的造型。": "Yue Fei, the celebrated patriotic Song-dynasty general, was said to be a reincarnation of the celestial Great Peng Star. His helmet therefore bears the form of a great peng bird with outspread wings.",
  "二郎神，又称：川主、显圣二郎真君、昭惠灵显王、灌口二郎、二郎真君、灌江神、赤城王、清源妙道真君。是中国民间和道教的神祇人物。民间多认为他是一位与水利、农耕、防止水灾、旱灾有关的神，甚至是水神。一般认为二郎神居于四川灌县（今都江堰市）。二郎神信仰起源于唐朝之前四川地区对于秦蜀郡太守李冰的信仰崇拜，并在北宋时期便流行于全中国。": "Erlang Shen, a deity of Chinese folk belief and Daoism, is also called Lord of Sichuan, Manifestly Holy Perfect Lord Erlang, King of Manifest Beneficence and Spiritual Efficacy, Guankou Erlang, Perfect Lord Erlang, Guanjiang Deity, King of Chicheng, and Perfect Lord of Pure Origin and Wondrous Dao. He is widely associated with irrigation, farming and protection from floods and droughts, and is sometimes considered a water deity. He is generally believed to reside in Guan County, Sichuan, now Dujiangyan. His worship grew from Sichuan’s pre-Tang veneration of Li Bing, Qin governor of Shu Commandery, and had spread throughout China by the Northern Song.",
  "该面具为贵州傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Guizhou Nuo theater or ritual, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "汉朝将军，其身世民间有两种说法，一说他是天上的菖蒲星，一说他是刘邦手下大将樊哙。在法事\"统兵回山\"中出场，职司是检查阴兵所收魂是否已经交给失魂人。来历 当代道真傩戏面具汉朝将军是一件由贵州省民族博物馆通过征集而来的民族历史和文化藏品。面具。": "General of the Han Dynasty. Two folk accounts explain his identity: one calls him the celestial Changpu Star, while another identifies him as Fan Kuai, a general under Liu Bang. He appears in the ritual ‘Leading the Troops Back to the Mountain,’ checking whether souls collected by spirit soldiers have been returned to those who lost them. Provenance: the contemporary Daozhen Nuo mask General of the Han Dynasty is an object of ethnic history and culture acquired by the Guizhou Provincial Museum of Ethnology.",
  "汉朝将军，是刘邦手下大将樊哙的化身。其该面具为武将造型，重在头冠的装饰，立眉竖眼，大鼻子阔嘴，形象十分威猛。": "The General of the Han Dynasty is an incarnation of Fan Kuai, a general under Liu Bang. His mask takes a martial form, emphasizing an ornate headdress, upright brows and staring eyes, a large nose and broad mouth, creating a forceful appearance.",
  "该面具对应民间信仰中的神祇角色，多与护佑地方、祈福禳灾、风雨收成或仪式迎神有关。": "This mask corresponds to a deity in folk belief, often associated with local protection, blessings and the averting of disaster, weather and harvests, or ritual welcomes for deities.",
  "年代 清 类别 少数民族工艺 其他“开路” “开路先锋贵州傩戏面具 傩戏开路面具 高清图 开路将军 又称开路先锋。": "Date: Qing dynasty. Category: ethnic minority craft. Other names: Road Opener, Road-Opening Vanguard, General Who Opens the Way. A Guizhou Nuo theater mask; the original record includes a high-resolution image label.",
  "和尚，是从佛教引进的角色，各地傩坛根据演出的需要，称谓各有不同，如\"九州和尚\"、\"扫地和尚\"、\"检斋和尚\"、\"减灾和尚\"等等。由于和尚面具的造型多为秃头圆脸，嘻牙咧嘴，慈眉善目，和蔼可亲，笑容可掬，额头上长着一个硕大的福包，形象亲切可爱，因此，也称之为“笑和尚”。在冲傩活动中，和尚专职负责检查监督还愿东家酬神的心愿是否真诚，各项供祭的物品、各项祭仪是否达到诸神要求的标准。其实，这些都是走过场，理性“公事”。和尚滑稽的表演和幽默的言辞，倒赢得围观者的阵阵喝彩。": "The Monk is a character adopted from Buddhism. Different Nuo traditions give him names according to performance needs, including Monk of the Nine Provinces, Sweeping Monk, Offering-Inspecting Monk and Disaster-Reducing Monk. His mask typically has a bald head, round face, exposed teeth in a broad smile, kindly brows and eyes, and a large auspicious swelling on the forehead. This friendly, endearing image also gives him the name Laughing Monk. In Chong Nuo activities, he checks whether the host is sincere in fulfilling vows and whether offerings and rituals meet the deities’ requirements. The source describes these inspections as largely ceremonial official business; his comic performance and humorous speech earn cheers from onlookers.",
  "魔礼寿地戏面具是一件由贵州省民族博物馆通过征集。魔礼寿，长约二丈四尺，武器为双锏。仙宠为紫金花狐貂，花狐貂平时呆在豹皮囊中，看上去像只白鼠，但战斗现身时大如白象，且生出双翼。魔礼寿是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，魔家四将之一，手持双锏，囊里有一物，形如白鼠，名曰花狐貂，放起空中，现身似白象，肋生飞翅，吃人无数。[1]后杨戬杀死花狐貂，并化身花狐貂为内应，助黄天化将其铲除。死后被封神为四大天王之东方持国天王，职顺。": "The Mo Lishou Dixi mask was acquired by the Guizhou Provincial Museum of Ethnology. Mo Lishou is described as about two zhang and four chi tall and armed with two metal truncheons. His magical pet, the purple-and-gold Huahu Diao, normally stays in a leopard-skin pouch looking like a white mouse; in battle it becomes as large as a white elephant and grows wings. Mo Lishou is one of the four Mo-family generals in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods. He releases the creature into the air, where it assumes its elephant-sized, winged form and devours many people. Yang Jian kills it, assumes its appearance and acts as an insider to help Huang Tianhua defeat Mo Lishou. After death, Mo Lishou is invested as Dhritarashtra, Heavenly King of the East, one of the Four Heavenly Kings, with responsibility for harmony and favorable conditions.",
  "彝族火把节流行于云南、贵州、四川等彝族地区的传统节日，国家级非物质文化遗产之一。火把节的起源与人们对火的崇拜有关，其目的是期望用火驱虫除害，保护庄稼生长。": "The Yi Torch Festival is a traditional festival practiced in Yi communities in Yunnan, Guizhou, Sichuan and elsewhere, and is recognized on the national intangible cultural heritage list. Its origins are associated with the veneration of fire and the hope that fire will drive away pests and protect crops.",
  "前言：搓泰吉是贵州威宁县裸嘎村特有的祭祀活动，一共用到五张面具。《中国面具艺术》• 彝族“搓泰吉面具 1 阿布摩（彝族老人 1700岁) 2 麻洪摩（苗族老人 1200岁这种源自贵州省威宁县裸嘎村的古老祭祀活动，不仅承载着彝族先民对自然、祖先的敬畏与崇拜，更是中华民族多元一体文化格局中不可或缺的一部分。在此，我们深入探讨《中国面具艺术》一书中关于彝族“撮泰吉面具的记述，感受其背后的历史沉淀与现代传承。": "Introduction: Cuotaiji is a sacrificial tradition distinctive to Luoga Village, Weining County, Guizhou, using five masks. Chinese Mask Art lists Yi Cuotaiji masks including Abumo, the Yi Elder aged 1,700, and Mahongmo, the Miao Elder aged 1,200. This ancient ritual from Luoga carries the Yi ancestors’ reverence for nature and ancestors and forms part of China’s culturally diverse heritage. The source introduces a closer discussion of the book’s account of these masks and their history and present-day transmission.",
  "狗是看家护院的，狗是由狼驯化而来的，早在狩猎采集时代，人们就已驯养狗为狩猎时的助手。因此，狗算是人类最早驯养的家畜。地域特色：广西桂林市曾是中国傩文化非常繁荣的地方，宋朝时期桂林制作的傩面具更是名震京城。面具。": "Dogs guard the home. Domesticated from wolves, they were already trained as hunting companions in the hunter-gatherer period and are therefore among humanity’s earliest domestic animals. Regional context: Guilin, Guangxi, was once a flourishing center of Chinese Nuo culture; masks made there in the Song dynasty were renowned even in the imperial capital.",
  "撮泰吉”（cuō tài jí）系贵州威宁彝族回族苗族自治县板底乡彝语的音译，现在见到的文字音译名称有撮衬姐、撮寸几、撮屯姐、撮特基、撮泰吉等十余种。演出节目：彝族撮泰吉的代表剧目有《变人戏》、《扫火星》、《耕耘舞蹈》等。演出时间：表演形式 【撮泰吉】一般在每年农历正月初三到十五演出,旨在驱邪崇、迎吉祥、祈丰收。": "Cuotaiji (cuō tài jí) transliterates a Yi term from Bandi Township, Weining Yi, Hui and Miao Autonomous County, Guizhou. More than ten written transliterations occur, including Cuochenjie, Cuocunji, Cuotunjie, Cuoteji and Cuotaiji. Representative pieces include The Drama of Becoming Human, Sweeping the Fire Stars and the Farming Dance. Performances generally take place from the third to the fifteenth day of the first lunar month, to expel evil, welcome good fortune and pray for a plentiful harvest.",
  "马华光又称灵官马元帅傩戏面具， 华光，又称灵官马元帅、华光天王、华光大帝、三眼灵光、马天君等，系道教护法四圣之一。": "Ma Huaguang, also known as Divine Officer Marshal Ma, a Nuo theater mask. Huaguang is also called Heavenly King Huaguang, Emperor Huaguang, Three-Eyed Lingguang and Heavenly Lord Ma. He is one of Daoism’s Four Guardian Saints.",
  "唐、葛、周三元面具均采用正神面相造型， 唐、葛、周三元面具均采用正神面相造型。": "The masks of the Three Yuan deities Tang, Ge and Zhou all use the facial form of principal deities. The original record repeats this description.",
  "广西地域的傩面“歪嘴和尚” 和尚这个角色在各地傩坛戏剧中都有出现，根据演出的需要和司职的区别，称谓各有不同，如\"九州和尚\"、\"扫地和尚\"、\"检斋和尚\"、\"减灾和尚\"等等。": "Crooked-Mouthed Monk, a Nuo mask from Guangxi. Monk characters appear in Nuo theater in many places. Depending on their performance role and duties, they are variously called Monk of the Nine Provinces, Sweeping Monk, Offering-Inspecting Monk, Disaster-Reducing Monk and other names.",
  "阿布摩 阿布是爷爷，摩是长者、智者，阿布摩意为老爷爷，1700岁，戴白胡须面具，是撮泰吉的核心人物，是领导者。他带领阿达姆、麻哄摩、嘿布背着谷种从遥远的勾凑发嘎迁徙到威宁倮嘎，一路战天斗地，克服困难，历尽沧桑，最终获得丰收，挽救人民。": "Abumo: abu means grandfather, while mo means an elder or wise person. The name means ‘Grandfather.’ Aged 1,700 and wearing a white-bearded mask, he is the central figure and leader of Cuotaiji. Carrying grain seed, he leads Adamu, Mahongmo and Heibu from distant Goucou Faga to Luoga in Weining. After struggling with the elements, overcoming hardship and enduring many trials, they finally secure a plentiful harvest and save the people.",
  "湘西地区的傩公傩母像， 傩公傩母是傩俗信仰中至高无上、最具威望的傩神,也是现代傩神信仰中的重要神明。作用：任何一坛傩戏都首先要在傩堂正中供奉傩公傩母，才能保佑这坛傩戏顺利进行，也才能达到主家的目的。": "Images of Nuo Gong and Nuo Mu from western Hunan. In Nuo folk belief they are supreme, highly revered Nuo deities and remain important in contemporary Nuo devotion. Before any Nuo performance cycle, they must be enshrined at the center of the ritual hall to protect its smooth progress and help fulfill the host’s purpose.",
  "提示：从左到自由分别是方相氏、傩王、雷公，由恩施市三岔镇鸦沐羽村傩面具制作传承人汪儒斌制作。方相氏是商周时期主持驱疫避邪仪式的神祇，掌蒙熊皮、黄金四目是其特点，这也是面具上有2双眼睛的原因。可以说，方相氏是傩戏起源开始就存在的典型形象。绿面的雷公就是雷震子，在傩戏中广泛，而面目更为狰狞的傩王则很好地表现出了传统恩施傩面具“以恶制恶的特色。除了世界技能博物馆外，方相氏和雷公两个造型的傩面具，也被中国工艺美术馆收藏。": "From left to right: Fangxiangshi, the Nuo King and the Thunder God, made by Wang Rubin, an inheritor of Nuo mask making from Yamuyu Village, Sancha Town, Enshi. Fangxiangshi is described as the divine figure presiding over epidemic-expelling and evil-averting rites in the Shang and Zhou periods. A bearskin and four golden eyes are defining attributes, explaining the mask’s two pairs of eyes. He is thus presented as a characteristic figure present from Nuo’s earliest origins. The green-faced Thunder God is Lei Zhenzi, widely represented in Nuo theater. The more ferocious Nuo King expresses Enshi masks’ traditional principle of ‘using evil to overcome evil.’ Besides the WorldSkills Museum, the China National Arts and Crafts Museum also holds masks in the Fangxiangshi and Thunder God forms.",
  "收藏于恩施州博物馆中的吊颈鬼， 吊颈鬼，又称缢鬼，顾名思义是被绳索吊死的人变成的鬼，一般为自杀或“绞刑的人。当然这是传说，暂时没有科学依据证明。展出地点：恩施州博物馆 价值和意义：面具不仅是傩戏艺术的表征，还体现了傩文化中的原始崇拜意识、民族意识和民俗意识。": "The Hanged Ghost, held by Enshi Prefecture Museum, is also called the Strangled Ghost. In folklore, it is the ghost of someone who died by hanging, usually through suicide or execution. This is a legend, and there is no scientific evidence establishing it. Exhibition location: Enshi Prefecture Museum. Significance: masks are not only expressions of Nuo theater but also embody early worship, ethnic identity and folk custom within Nuo culture.",
  "收藏于恩施州博物馆中的阴阳太， 介绍 展出地点：恩施州博物馆 价值和意义：面具不仅是傩戏艺术的表征，还体现了傩文化中的原始崇拜意识、民族意识和民俗意识。": "Yinyang Tai, held by Enshi Prefecture Museum. Exhibition location: Enshi Prefecture Museum. Significance: masks are not only expressions of Nuo theater but also embody early worship, ethnic identity and folk custom within Nuo culture.",
  "收藏于恩施州博物馆中的傩戏面具雷震子， 雷震子是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，天雷将星下世，在雷雨中出生，被奔赴朝歌途中的周文王姬昌在燕山收为养子，乃文王姬昌第一百子，后成为阐教门人云中子的徒弟。展出地点：恩施州博物馆 价值和意义：面具不仅是傩戏艺术的表征，还体现了傩文化中的原始崇拜意识、民族意识和民俗意识。": "Lei Zhenzi Nuo theater mask, held by Enshi Prefecture Museum. Lei Zhenzi is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods, a celestial thunder-general star descended to earth. Born during a thunderstorm, he is adopted on Mount Yan by Ji Chang, King Wen of Zhou, while the latter travels to Chaoge. He becomes Ji Chang’s hundredth son and later a disciple of the Chan sect immortal Yunzhongzi. Exhibition location: Enshi Prefecture Museum. Significance: masks are not only expressions of Nuo theater but also embody early worship, ethnic identity and folk custom within Nuo culture.",
  "收藏于恩施州博物馆中的猪八戒、牛王、方弼、杨任傩面具， 猪八戒，又名猪刚鬣、猪悟能，是古典名著《西游记》中的人物。牛王在民间信仰中被视为牛的保护神。据传，牛王能保护耕牛免受瘟疫侵害，因此古代农家常供奉之。方弼：方相、方弼兄弟二人是商朝殷纣王的两位镇殿将军。自古就被西北民间誉为“把门的将军”。杨任是明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，本是商朝的大夫，阐教玉虚三代传人之一。展出地点：恩施州博物馆 价值和意义：面具不仅是傩戏艺术的表征，还体现了傩文化中的原始崇拜意识、民族意识和民俗意识。": "Nuo masks of Zhu Bajie, the Ox King, Fang Bi and Yang Ren, held by Enshi Prefecture Museum. Zhu Bajie, also named Zhu Ganglie or Zhu Wuneng, is a character in Journey to the West. In folk belief, the Ox King protects cattle; farmers traditionally worshipped him in the hope of protecting working oxen from disease. Fang Bi and his brother Fang Xiang are two palace-guard generals of King Zhou of Shang, long called ‘the generals who guard the gate’ in northwestern folk tradition. Yang Ren is a character in Investiture of the Gods, originally a Shang official and one of the Chan sect’s third-generation Jade Void disciples. Exhibition location: Enshi Prefecture Museum. Significance: masks express Nuo theater and embody early worship, ethnic identity and folk custom within Nuo culture.",
  "收藏于恩施州博物馆中的斗口灵官马元帅傩面具， 斗口灵官马天君马天君，名胜，字德先，道经中称「正一魁神灵官马元帅」。白面美髯，头戴方角幞头，身着黄短绣衫，右手持枪，枪上有白蛇缠绕。展出地点：恩施州博物馆 价值和意义：面具不仅是傩戏艺术的表征，还体现了傩文化中的原始崇拜意识、民族意识和民俗意识。": "Doukou Divine Officer Marshal Ma Nuo mask, held by Enshi Prefecture Museum. Heavenly Lord Ma, personal name Sheng and courtesy name Dexian, is called ‘Zhengyi Chief Deity and Divine Officer Marshal Ma’ in Daoist texts. He has a fair face and a fine beard, wears a square-cornered futou headpiece and a short yellow embroidered robe, and holds a spear in his right hand with a white snake coiled around it. Exhibition location: Enshi Prefecture Museum. Significance: masks are not only expressions of Nuo theater but also embody early worship, ethnic identity and folk custom within Nuo culture.",
  "乡约 恩施土家族木质傩面具 乡约是指在乡里中订立的需要乡民共同遵守的规约，同时也指奉官命在乡里中管事的人，由县官任命，负责传达政令、调解纠纷等职责。乡约大概相当于现在的乡长、镇长,乡约相当于管辖几个村的村长。": "Xiangyue, a wooden Tujia Nuo mask from Enshi. Xiangyue means a community compact whose rules villagers are expected to follow, and also an official appointed by a county magistrate to manage local affairs, convey government orders and mediate disputes. The role is roughly comparable to a township head or a village chief responsible for several villages.",
  "恩施木质傩面具角色“笑罗汉”， 笑罗汉是十八罗汉的第二尊欢喜罗汉的别称。代表着“法喜充满”。欢喜罗汉，即迦诺迦代蹉尊者，是当时著名的论师。": "Laughing Arhat, a wooden Nuo mask character from Enshi. Laughing Arhat is another name for the Joyful Arhat, the second of the Eighteen Arhats, expressing ‘joy filled with the Dharma.’ The Joyful Arhat, the venerable Kanakavatsa, was a renowned expounder of Buddhist teachings.",
  "天门土地”，恩施三岔木傩面具。该面具对应民间信仰中的神祇角色，多与护佑地方、祈福禳灾、风雨收成或仪式迎神有关。": "Earth God of the Heavenly Gate, a wooden Nuo mask from Sancha, Enshi. This mask corresponds to a deity in folk belief, often associated with local protection, blessings and the averting of disaster, weather and harvests, or ritual welcomes for deities.",
  "铁匠傩戏面具， 铁匠也是一门古老的职业，他们以铁为原料，靠一把小小的铁锤打造出各式各样的生产工具和生活用品。": "Blacksmith Nuo theater mask. Blacksmithing is an ancient trade: using iron and a small hammer, blacksmiths forge a variety of tools and everyday objects.",
  "歪嘴和尚恩施近代木质傩面具。该面具表现佛教人物或僧侣形象，常用于呈现慈和、诙谐或劝善意味的角色。": "Crooked-Mouthed Monk, a modern-period wooden Nuo mask from Enshi. This mask depicts a Buddhist figure or monk, often conveying gentleness, humor or encouragement to do good.",
  "该面具为湖北恩施傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Nuo theater or ritual in Enshi, Hubei, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "城隍，有的地方又称城隍爷，是中国古代宗教文化中普遍崇祀的重要神祇之一，大多由有功于地方民众的名臣英雄充当，是中国民间和道教信奉守护城池之神。": "Chenghuang, also called the City God, is an important deity widely worshipped in traditional Chinese religious culture. Usually identified with a distinguished official or hero who served local people, he is honored in folk belief and Daoism as the guardian of a city.",
  "黄花夫人恩施地区木质傩戏面具，由本站。": "Lady Huanghua, a wooden Nuo theater mask from the Enshi area. The original record ends with an incomplete reference to this website.",
  "判官在阴间则是传说中的阴间官名，职责是判处人的轮回生死，对坏人进行惩罚，对好人进行奖励。阴间的判官通常被描绘成长相凶神恶煞但心地善良正直的形象，下辖赏善司、罚恶司、察查司、阴律司等职位。": "The Judge is an official of the underworld in legend, responsible for decisions about death, rebirth, punishment for wrongdoing and rewards for good conduct. Underworld judges are usually portrayed with fierce appearances but kind, upright hearts. Their offices include rewarding good, punishing evil, investigation and the laws of the underworld.",
  "该面具带有兽形、驱邪或原始祭仪意味，常通过夸张的口鼻、眼部和轮廓表现威慑力。": "This mask carries animal, exorcistic or early ritual associations. Exaggerated mouths, noses, eyes and outlines often convey an intimidating presence.",
  "方弼是商朝殷纣王的两位镇殿将军。方相、方弼兄弟二人自古就被西北民间誉为“把门的将军”。": "Fang Bi is one of King Zhou of Shang’s two palace-guard generals. He and his brother Fang Xiang have long been known in northwestern folk tradition as ‘the generals who guard the gate.’",
  "恩施地区“关济相公傩面。该面具为湖北恩施傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "Lord Guanji, a Nuo mask from Enshi. A character mask from Nuo theater or ritual in Enshi, Hubei, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "雷震子，明代神魔小说《封神演义》中的人物，周文王姬昌的第一百子（养子）、阐教门人云中子的徒弟、玉虚第三代弟子、西周武将之一。": "Lei Zhenzi is a character in the Ming-dynasty fantasy novel Investiture of the Gods: the hundredth, adopted son of Ji Chang, King Wen of Zhou; a disciple of the Chan sect immortal Yunzhongzi; a third-generation Jade Void disciple; and a Western Zhou military commander.",
  "杨泗为读书人，在傩戏中，亲说家史为湖北恩州府杨家坪村人。": "Yang Si is a scholar. In Nuo theater, he recounts his family history as a native of Yangjiaping Village, Enzhou Prefecture, Hubei.",
  "虎头吞口 虎头吞口主要有葫芦瓢画和木雕两类。一般都带有一柄长把，依旧保持勺柄状。彝族毕摩用葫芦瓢绘制吞口时，总是设法突出其猛虎的特征，创造一种惟彝族独有的“五虎吞口”。即在一个大虎头内含有四个小虎头，额头上面一个、两只眼珠各长一个，口中咬的剑柄头也雕成虎头形状。彝族认为，虎头吞口以虎年、虎月、虎日、虎时所画，在虎日悬挂最能灵验。有些地方的彝族甚至在举行祭祖大典时，把虎头挂于门楣上，加以祭祀，并表示这家人是虎的子孙，正在祭祖。文山彝族的虎头吞口多为陶泥捏塑后置于瓦窑中烧成，置于屋顶，形态狰狞。面具。": "Tiger-head Tunkou occur mainly as painted gourd ladles or wood carvings, usually with a long handle retaining the shape of a spoon. When Yi bimo ritual specialists paint them on gourd ladles, they emphasize the fierce tiger and create a distinctive ‘Five-Tiger Tunkou’: a large tiger head containing four smaller heads, one on the forehead, one on each eyeball, and one forming the hilt of the sword held in the mouth. In Yi belief, a tiger-head Tunkou painted in the tiger year, month, day and hour, then hung on a tiger day, is most efficacious. Some Yi communities hang a tiger head above the door and make offerings during major ancestor rites, indicating that the household are descendants of the tiger and are worshipping their ancestors. In Wenshan, Yi tiger-head Tunkou are often modeled from clay, fired in tile kilns and placed on rooftops, with fierce forms.",
  "木雕《茶圣陆羽》 祁门傩舞面具 谢润华作品。陆羽(约733-约804)，字鸿渐，唐朝复州竟陵(今湖北天门市)人。一名疾，字季疵，号竟陵子、桑苎翁、 东冈子，又号\"茶山御史\"。唐代茶学家，被誉为\"茶仙\"，尊为\"茶圣\"，祀为\"茶神\"。": "Wood carving, Lu Yu, the Sage of Tea, a Qimen Nuo dance mask by Xie Runhua. Lu Yu (c. 733–c. 804), courtesy name Hongjian, came from Jingling in Fuzhou during the Tang, now Tianmen, Hubei. He also used the personal name Ji and courtesy name Jici, and the sobriquets Jinglingzi, Sangzhu Weng, Donggangzi and ‘Censor of Tea Mountain.’ A Tang scholar of tea, he was praised as a Tea Immortal, honored as the Sage of Tea and worshipped as the Tea God.",
  "该面具为湖南湘西傩戏或傩仪中的角色面具，主要用于仪式表演、迎神还愿或民间信仰叙事。": "A character mask from Nuo theater or ritual in western Hunan, mainly used in ritual performances, deity-welcoming and vow-fulfillment activities, or narratives of folk belief.",
  "貂蝉，湘西侗族傩戏中有关公捉貂蝉的三国戏。貂蝉（生卒年不详），历史小说《三国演义》中的人物，是中国古代四大美女(西施,王昭君,貂蝉,杨玉环)之一。在民间传说中她原名任红昌，也有人认为吕布部将秦宜禄前妻杜夫人（杜秀娘）即是貂蝉。她为了报答义父王允的养育之恩而甘愿献身完成连环计的故事在民间广为流传。貂蝉是中国民间传说中的美女，也曾登场于历史小说《三国演义》，民间传说为山西忻州人，与名将关羽为同乡，出生于河南洛阳。与西施、杨玉环、王昭君并称中国古代四大美女。在民间传说中她原名任红昌，是山西一村姑，也有人认为吕布部将秦宜禄前妻杜氏(杜秀娘)即是貂蝉。当代著名作家朱千华先生在其人文地理著作《中国美女地理》中，对貂蝉的原型、身世等，有详细的考证。": "Diaochan appears in a Three Kingdoms play about Lord Guan capturing her in Dong Nuo theater in western Hunan. A character in the historical novel Romance of the Three Kingdoms, with unknown birth and death dates, she is counted among China’s Four Beauties alongside Xi Shi, Wang Zhaojun and Yang Yuhuan. In folk legend her original name is Ren Hongchang; another interpretation identifies her with Lady Du, or Du Xiuniang, the former wife of Lü Bu’s subordinate Qin Yilu. The widely told story describes her willingness to carry out a chain of stratagems to repay her adoptive father Wang Yun for raising her. Folk accounts identify her as a woman from Xinzhou, Shanxi, a fellow provincial of Guan Yu, while also giving Luoyang, Henan, as her birthplace. Other versions describe Ren Hongchang as a Shanxi village girl. The modern writer Zhu Qianhua examines her possible historical model and background in detail in his cultural-geography book The Geography of Chinese Beauties."
});
